#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:944
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Blocks written before the expansion keep their old data-to-parity ratio and "
"continue to occupy space accordingly.  The full capacity gain from the new "
"disk therefore applies to data written after the expansion, while old data "
"benefits only when rewritten, for example with crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-rewrite,"
"`zfs rewrite`].  Repeat the procedure to grow a vdev by several disks, "
"attaching one at a time."
msgstr "扩展前写入的数据块会保留原有的数据与校验比例，并相应地继续占用空间。因此，新磁盘带来的全部容量增益仅适用于扩展后写入的数据；旧数据只有在重写后才能受益，例如使用 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-rewrite,`zfs rewrite`]。重复此过程，每次添加一块磁盘，即可为 vdev 添加多块磁盘。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:946
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "dRAID Pools"
msgstr "dRAID 池"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:953
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"dRAID is a variant of RAID-Z that distributes hot spare capacity across all "
"disks in the vdev.  A crossref:zfs[zfs-term-vdev-draid,dRAID] vdev is built "
"from internal RAID-Z groups plus optional _distributed spares_, all spread "
"evenly over every disk.  When a disk fails, ZFS rebuilds into the "
"distributed spare by reading from and writing to all remaining disks in "
"parallel, completing in a fraction of the time a resilver onto a single "
"spare disk takes.  Replacing the failed disk then rebuilds it from the "
"distributed spare, restoring full protection.  dRAID targets pools with many "
"disks, where RAID-Z rebuild times grow dangerously long."
msgstr "dRAID 是 RAID-Z 的一种变体，它将热备用容量分布到 vdev 中的所有磁盘上。crossref:zfs[zfs-term-vdev-draid,dRAID] vdev 由内部 RAID-Z 组和可选的 __分布式备用空间__ 构成，所有部分均匀分布在每块磁盘上。磁盘发生故障时，ZFS 会从所有剩余磁盘并行读取并写入分布式备用空间，以重建数据；所需时间仅为重建到单块备用磁盘的一小部分。更换故障磁盘后，ZFS 会从分布式备用空间重建该磁盘，从而恢复完整保护。dRAID 面向磁盘数量较多的池，在这类池中，RAID-Z 的重建时间会变得过长，带来严重风险。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:955
#, fuzzy
msgid "The vdev type spells out the complete layout, per man:zpoolconcepts[7]:"
msgstr "vdev 类型会完整说明布局，详见 man:zpoolconcepts[7]："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:959
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "draid[parity][:datad][:childrenc][:sparess]\n"
msgstr "draid[parity][:datad][:childrenc][:sparess]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:965
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"_parity_ is the parity level of the internal groups, 1 to 3, defaulting to "
"1.  _data_ is the number of data devices per redundancy group, defaulting to "
"8.  _children_ is the total number of disks, serving as a cross-check when "
"listing many devices.  _spares_ is the number of distributed hot spares, "
"defaulting to 0."
msgstr "__校验级别__是内部组的校验级别，范围为 1 到 3，默认值为 1。__数据盘数__是每个冗余组中的数据设备数量，默认值为 8。__子设备数__是磁盘总数，在列出大量设备时可用于交叉核对。__备用盘数__是分布式热备用盘的数量，默认值为 0。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:967
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Create a pool from a 24-disk dRAID vdev with double parity, 8 data disks per "
"redundancy group, and 2 distributed spares:"
msgstr "使用由 24 块磁盘组成的 dRAID vdev 创建池，其中采用双重校验，每个冗余组有 8 块数据盘和 2 个分布式备用盘："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:971
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool create mypool draid2:8d:24c:2s ada0 ada1 ada2 ada3 ada4 ada5 ada6 ada7 ada8 ada9 ada10 ada11 ada12 ada13 ada14 ada15 ada16 ada17 ada18 ada19 ada20 ada21 ada22 ada23\n"
msgstr "# zpool create mypool draid2:8d:24c:2s ada0 ada1 ada2 ada3 ada4 ada5 ada6 ada7 ada8 ada9 ada10 ada11 ada12 ada13 ada14 ada15 ada16 ada17 ada18 ada19 ada20 ada21 ada22 ada23\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:974
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The distributed spares appear under `spares` in `zpool status`, with names "
"like `draid2-0-0` for the first spare of the first vdev."
msgstr "分布式备用盘会显示在 `zpool status` 的 `spares` 下；第一个 vdev 的第一个备用盘会使用类似 `draid2-0-0` 的名称。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:981
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"dRAID trades space efficiency for rebuild speed.  Unlike RAID-Z, dRAID uses "
"a fixed stripe width, padding smaller writes with zeros.  With the default "
"of 8 data disks and 4 KB sectors, the minimum allocation is 32 KB, which "
"reduces usable capacity and compression effectiveness for datasets dominated "
"by small blocks.  The capacity of the distributed spares is also committed "
"up front, whether or not a disk ever fails.  Pairing a dRAID pool with a "
"crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-special,special vdev] keeps metadata and small blocks "
"off the wide stripes and recovers much of the lost efficiency.  For pools "
"with a handful of disks, RAID-Z remains the better choice."
msgstr "dRAID 以空间效率换取重建速度。与 RAID-Z 不同，dRAID 使用固定的条带宽度，并以零填充较小的写入。使用默认的 8 块数据盘和 4 KB 扇区时，最小分配单位为 32 KB；对于以小数据块为主的数据集，这会降低可用容量和压缩效率。无论磁盘是否发生故障，分布式备用盘的容量也会预先占用。将 dRAID 池与 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-special,special vdev] 配合使用，可将元数据和小数据块移出宽条带，从而恢复大部分损失的效率。对于只有少量磁盘的池，RAID-Z 仍是更好的选择。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:983
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Special Allocation Classes"
msgstr "特殊分配类"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:989
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Special allocation classes dedicate vdevs to specific types of pool data.  A "
"crossref:zfs[zfs-term-vdev-special,special] vdev stores pool metadata such "
"as indirect blocks and dnodes, and optionally the data blocks of small "
"files.  A `dedup` vdev stores the crossref:zfs[zfs-term-deduplication,"
"deduplication] tables.  Placing this metadata on fast devices such as NVMe "
"mirrors speeds up metadata-heavy operations like directory traversal, `zfs "
"list`, and deduplication lookups on pools of otherwise slower disks."
msgstr "特殊分配类会将 vdev 专用于存储特定类型的池数据。crossref:zfs[zfs-term-vdev-special,special] vdev 用于存储池元数据，例如间接块和 dnode，也可选择存储小文件的数据块。`dedup` vdev 用于存储 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-deduplication,去重]表。将这些元数据放在 NVMe 镜像等快速设备上，可加快目录遍历、`zfs list` 和去重查询等元数据密集型操作，即使池中的其他磁盘速度较慢也能如此。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:991
#, fuzzy
msgid "Add a mirrored special vdev to an existing pool:"
msgstr "向现有池添加镜像 special vdev："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:995
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool add mypool special mirror nda0 nda1\n"
msgstr "# zpool add mypool special mirror nda0 nda1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:998
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"New metadata allocations then go to the special vdev; existing metadata "
"stays where it is until rewritten."
msgstr "此后新分配的元数据会写入 special vdev；已有元数据仍保留在原处，直到被重写。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1000
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Setting the `special_small_blocks` dataset property makes the special vdev "
"store data blocks up to the given size as well:"
msgstr "设置数据集属性 `special_small_blocks`，即可让 special vdev 也存储不超过指定大小的数据块："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1004
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zfs set special_small_blocks=16K mypool/projects\n"
msgstr "# zfs set special_small_blocks=16K mypool/projects\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1009
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Valid values are zero, which disables storing data blocks in the special "
"class, or a power of two from 512 bytes up to 1 MB on FreeBSD 14.x; FreeBSD "
"15.0 accepts values up to the maximum block size of 16 MB.  Setting the "
"property to the dataset's `recordsize` sends all data blocks of that dataset "
"to the special class.  When a special vdev fills up, new allocations spill "
"back to the normal class instead of failing."
msgstr "有效值可以是零（表示不在 special 类中存储数据块），也可以是 512 字节到 1 MB 之间的 2 的幂；在 FreeBSD 14.x 上适用此范围。FreeBSD 15.0 接受的值可达到 16 MB 的最大块大小。将该属性设为数据集的 `recordsize`，会把该数据集的所有数据块都发送到 special 类。special vdev 空间用满时，新的分配会转回普通类，而不会失败。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1015
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A special vdev is not a cache.  It holds the only copy of the pool metadata "
"allocated to it, and losing it destroys the pool.  Match the redundancy of "
"special and dedup vdevs to the redundancy of the data vdevs, for example by "
"using a mirror."
msgstr "special vdev 不是缓存。它保存分配给它的池元数据的唯一副本；丢失该 vdev 会导致池损毁。special 和 dedup vdev 的冗余级别应与数据 vdev 的冗余级别相匹配，例如使用镜像。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1019
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Removing a special or dedup vdev with `zpool remove` is possible, subject to "
"the restrictions described in crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-attach,Adding and "
"Removing Devices].  In practice, the matching `ashift` requirement often "
"prevents removal when the special vdev uses devices with a different sector "
"size than the data vdevs."
msgstr "可以使用 `zpool remove` 移除 special 或 dedup vdev，但须遵守 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-attach,添加和移除设备]中描述的限制。实际上，匹配 `ashift` 的要求常常会阻止移除操作，尤其是在 special vdev 使用的设备扇区大小与数据 vdev 不同时。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1021
#, no-wrap
msgid "Checking the Status of a Pool"
msgstr "检擦存储池状态"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1027
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Pool status is important.  If a drive goes offline or ZFS detects a read, "
"write, or checksum error, the corresponding error count increases.  The "
"`status` output shows the configuration and status of each device in the "
"pool and the status of the entire pool.  Actions to take and details about "
"the last crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-scrub,`scrub`] are also shown."
msgstr ""
"存储池的状态很重要，若有磁盘机离线或侦测到读取、写入或校验码（Checksum）错"
"误，对应的错误计数便会增加。 status 会显示存储池中每一个磁盘机的设定与状态及"
"整个存储池的状态。需要处置的方式与有关最近清洁（Scrub）S的详细资讯也会一并显"
"示。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1035
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool status\n"
"  pool: mypool\n"
" state: ONLINE\n"
"  scan: scrub repaired 0B in 02:25:36 with 0 errors on Sat Jul 11 06:51:26 2026\n"
"config:\n"
msgstr "# zpool status\n  pool: mypool\n state: ONLINE\n  scan: scrub repaired 0B in 02:25:36 with 0 errors on Sat Jul 11 06:51:26 2026\nconfig:\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1045
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1341
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"        NAME        STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n"
"        mypool      ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"          raidz2-0  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            ada0p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            ada1p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            ada2p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            ada3p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            ada4p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            ada5p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
msgstr "        NAME        STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n        mypool      ONLINE       0     0     0\n          raidz2-0  ONLINE       0     0     0\n            ada0p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n            ada1p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n            ada2p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n            ada3p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n            ada4p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n            ada5p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1050
#, fuzzy
msgid "Options adjust the output to the task at hand:"
msgstr "可根据当前任务调整输出选项："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1052
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`-v` displays verbose data error information, printing a complete list of "
"the errors found since the last complete pool scrub, including the names of "
"affected files."
msgstr "`-v` 显示详细的数据错误信息，列出上次完整池清理以来发现的所有错误，包括受影响文件的名称。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1053
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`-x` displays the status of pools with errors or pools that are otherwise "
"unavailable, hiding healthy pools."
msgstr "`-x` 显示存在错误或以其他方式不可用的池，并隐藏健康的池。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1054
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`-s` displays the number of slow I/O operations on each leaf vdev, meaning "
"operations that did not complete within 30 seconds."
msgstr "`-s` 显示每个叶级 vdev 上的慢速 I/O 操作数量，即未能在 30 秒内完成的操作。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1055
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`-e` displays unhealthy vdevs only, keeping the output short for pools with "
"many devices; this flag requires FreeBSD 14.1 or later."
msgstr "`-e` 仅显示不健康的 vdev，以缩短包含大量设备的池的输出；此标志要求 FreeBSD 14.1 或更高版本。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1056
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`-p` displays numbers as exact, parseable values instead of rounded human-"
"readable ones."
msgstr "`-p` 以精确、可解析的值显示数字，而不是经过四舍五入、便于阅读的值。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1057
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`-t` displays the crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-trim,TRIM] status of each vdev."
msgstr "`-t` 显示每个 vdev 的 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-trim,TRIM] 状态。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1059
#, fuzzy
msgid "Refer to man:zpool-status[8] for the complete list of options."
msgstr "完整选项列表请参阅 man:zpool-status[8]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1061
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clearing Errors"
msgstr "排除错误"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1067
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When detecting an error, ZFS increases the read, write, or checksum error "
"counts.  Clear the error message and reset the counts with `zpool clear "
"_mypool_`.  Clearing the error state can be important for automated scripts "
"that alert the administrator when the pool encounters an error.  Without "
"clearing old errors, the scripts may fail to report further errors."
msgstr "检测到错误时，ZFS 会增加读取、写入或校验和错误计数。使用 `zpool clear _mypool_` 清除错误消息并重置计数。清除错误状态对于自动脚本很重要；这类脚本会在池遇到错误时提醒管理员。如果不清除旧错误，脚本可能无法报告后续错误。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1069
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replacing a Functioning Device"
msgstr "更换正在运行的设备"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1078
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It may be desirable to replace one disk with a different disk.  When "
"replacing a working disk, the process keeps the old disk online during the "
"replacement.  The pool never enters a crossref:zfs[zfs-term-degraded,"
"degraded] state, reducing the risk of data loss.  Running `zpool replace` "
"copies the data from the old disk to the new one.  After the operation "
"completes, ZFS disconnects the old disk from the vdev.  If the new disk is "
"larger than the old disk, it may be possible to grow the zpool, using the "
"new space.  See crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-online,Growing a Pool]."
msgstr ""
"可能有一些情况会需要更换磁盘为另一个磁盘，当要更换运作中的磁盘，此程序会维持"
"旧有的磁盘在更换的过程为上线的状态，存储池不会进入降级（<link linkend=\"zfs-"
"term-degraded\">degraded</link>）的状态，来减少数据遗失的风险。"
"<command>zpool replace</command> 会复制所有旧磁盘的数据到新磁盘，操作完成之后"
"旧磁盘便会与 vdev 中断连线。若新磁盘容量较旧磁盘大，也可以会增加存储池来使用"
"新的空间，请参考 <link linkend=\"zfs-zpool-online\">扩展存储池</link>。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1080
msgid "Replace a functioning device in the pool:"
msgstr "更换存储池中正在运行的设备："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1097
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"errors: No known data errors\n"
"# zpool replace mypool ada1p3 ada2p3\n"
"Make sure to wait until resilvering finishes before rebooting.\n"
msgstr "errors: No known data errors\n# zpool replace mypool ada1p3 ada2p3\n请务必等待 resilver 完成后再重新启动。\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1099
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "When booting from the pool 'mypool', update the boot code on the newly attached disk 'ada2p3'.\n"
msgstr "如果从池 'mypool' 启动，请更新新连接磁盘 'ada2p3' 上的引导代码。\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1101
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Assuming GPT partitioning is used and ada0 is the new boot disk, use the following command:\n"
msgstr "假设使用 GPT 分区，并且 ada0 是新的启动磁盘，请使用以下命令：\n"

