#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1144
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On mirrored vdevs, adding `-s` to `zpool replace` or `zpool attach` performs "
"a _sequential resilver_ instead of a healing resilver.  A sequential "
"resilver copies the data in disk order without verifying each block "
"checksum, restoring redundancy much sooner.  Since the copy skips checksum "
"verification, ZFS starts a crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-scrub,scrub] of the pool "
"automatically after the sequential resilver completes.  Sequential "
"resilvering works on mirror and crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-draid,dRAID] vdevs, "
"not on RAID-Z.  Restart an in-progress resilver from the beginning with "
"`zpool resilver _mypool_`."
msgstr "对于镜像 vdev，在 `zpool replace` 或 `zpool attach` 中添加 `-s` 可执行__顺序 resilver__，而不是修复性 resilver。顺序 resilver 按磁盘顺序复制数据，不会逐块校验校验和，因此能更快恢复冗余。由于复制时跳过了校验和验证，顺序 resilver 完成后，ZFS 会自动对池执行 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-scrub,scrub]。顺序 resilver 适用于镜像和 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-draid,dRAID] vdev，不适用于 RAID-Z。使用 `zpool resilver _mypool_` 可从头开始重新执行正在进行的 resilver。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1146
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dealing with Failed Devices"
msgstr "处理故障设备"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1154
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When a disk in a pool fails, the vdev to which the disk belongs enters the "
"crossref:zfs[zfs-term-degraded,degraded] state.  The data is still "
"available, but with reduced performance because ZFS computes missing data "
"from the available redundancy.  To restore the vdev to a fully functional "
"state, replace the failed physical device.  ZFS is then instructed to begin "
"the crossref:zfs[zfs-term-resilver,resilver] operation.  ZFS recomputes data "
"on the failed device from available redundancy and writes it to the "
"replacement device.  After completion, the vdev returns to crossref:zfs[zfs-"
"term-online,online] status."
msgstr "池中的磁盘发生故障时，该磁盘所属的 vdev 会进入 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-degraded,降级]状态。数据仍然可用，但由于 ZFS 必须根据可用冗余计算缺失的数据，性能会降低。要使 vdev 恢复完全正常的状态，请更换故障物理设备。随后，ZFS 会开始 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-resilver,resilver] 操作。ZFS 根据可用冗余重新计算故障设备上的数据，并将其写入替换设备。完成后，vdev 会恢复为 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-online,在线]状态。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1157
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the vdev does not have any redundancy, or if devices have failed and "
"there is not enough redundancy to compensate, the pool enters the crossref:"
"zfs[zfs-term-faulted,faulted] state.  Unless enough devices can reconnect, "
"the pool becomes inoperative, requiring a data restore from backups."
msgstr ""
"若 vdev 没有任何备份数据或有多个设备故障，没有足够的备援数据可以补偿，存储便"
"会进入故障（<link linkend=\"zfs-term-faulted\">faulted</link>）的状态。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1160
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When replacing a failed disk, the name of the failed disk changes to the "
"GUID of the new disk.  A new device name parameter for `zpool replace` is "
"not required if the replacement device has the same device name."
msgstr "更换故障磁盘时，故障磁盘的名称会变为新磁盘的 GUID。如果替换设备的设备名称相同，则无需为 `zpool replace` 提供新的设备名称参数。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1162
#, fuzzy
msgid "Replace a failed disk using `zpool replace`:"
msgstr "使用 `zpool replace` 更换故障磁盘："

