#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1218
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Hot Spares and Automatic Replacement with zfsd"
msgstr "热备用盘和使用 zfsd 自动更换"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1223
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Pools with redundant vdevs can register crossref:zfs[zfs-term-vdev-spare,hot "
"spare] disks that stand by to replace a failed device.  A spare must be at "
"least as large as the device it replaces.  Specify spares at pool creation "
"time by listing them after the `spare` keyword, as in `zpool create _mypool_ "
"mirror _ada0p3_ _ada1p3_ spare _ada3p3_`, or add them to an existing pool "
"with `zpool add`:"
msgstr "包含冗余 vdev 的池可以注册 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-vdev-spare,热备用盘]，以便在设备故障时待命并替换故障设备。备用盘的容量不得小于被替换设备。创建池时，可在 `spare` 关键字后列出备用盘，例如 `zpool create _mypool_ mirror _ada0p3_ _ada1p3_ spare _ada3p3_`；也可以使用 `zpool add` 将备用盘添加到现有池："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1231
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool add mypool spare ada3p3\n"
"# zpool status\n"
"  pool: mypool\n"
" state: ONLINE\n"
"config:\n"
msgstr "# zpool add mypool spare ada3p3\n# zpool status\n  pool: mypool\n state: ONLINE\nconfig:\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1239
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"        NAME        STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n"
"        mypool      ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"          mirror-0  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            ada0p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            ada1p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"        spares\n"
"          ada3p3    AVAIL\n"
msgstr "        NAME        STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n        mypool      ONLINE       0     0     0\n          mirror-0  ONLINE       0     0     0\n            ada0p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n            ada1p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n        spares\n          ada3p3    AVAIL\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1245
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A spare stays idle, shown as `AVAIL`, until a device fails.  Activate a "
"spare by hand with `zpool replace`, naming the failed device and the spare:"
msgstr "备用盘会保持空闲，显示为 `AVAIL`，直到设备发生故障。使用 `zpool replace` 并指定故障设备和备用盘，即可手动启用备用盘："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1258
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool replace mypool ada1p3 ada3p3\n"
"# zpool status\n"
"  pool: mypool\n"
" state: DEGRADED\n"
"status: One or more devices could not be opened.  Sufficient replicas exist for\n"
"        the pool to continue functioning in a degraded state.\n"
"action: Attach the missing device and online it using 'zpool online'.\n"
"   see: https://openzfs.github.io/openzfs-docs/msg/ZFS-8000-2Q\n"
"  scan: resilvered 781M in 00:00:21 with 0 errors on Sat Jul 11 09:14:33 2026\n"
"config:\n"
msgstr "# zpool replace mypool ada1p3 ada3p3\n# zpool status\n  pool: mypool\n state: DEGRADED\nstatus: One or more devices could not be opened.  Sufficient replicas exist for\n        the pool to continue functioning in a degraded state.\naction: Attach the missing device and online it using 'zpool online'.\n   see: https://openzfs.github.io/openzfs-docs/msg/ZFS-8000-2Q\n  scan: resilvered 781M in 00:00:21 with 0 errors on Sat Jul 11 09:14:33 2026\nconfig:\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1268
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"        NAME          STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n"
"        mypool        DEGRADED     0     0     0\n"
"          mirror-0    DEGRADED     0     0     0\n"
"            ada0p3    ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            spare-1   DEGRADED     0     0     0\n"
"              ada1p3  UNAVAIL      0     0     0  cannot open\n"
"              ada3p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"        spares\n"
"          ada3p3      INUSE     currently in use\n"
msgstr "        NAME          STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n        mypool        DEGRADED     0     0     0\n          mirror-0    DEGRADED     0     0     0\n            ada0p3    ONLINE       0     0     0\n            spare-1   DEGRADED     0     0     0\n              ada1p3  UNAVAIL      0     0     0  cannot open\n              ada3p3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n        spares\n          ada3p3      INUSE     currently in use\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1275
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The spare replacement is temporary by design, and the pool stays in this "
"state until an administrator resolves it.  After physically replacing the "
"failed disk and resilvering the new device with crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-"
"replace,`zpool replace`], return the spare to standby with `zpool detach "
"_mypool_ _ada3p3_`.  To promote the spare to a permanent member of the vdev "
"instead, detach the failed device with `zpool detach _mypool_ _ada1p3_`."
msgstr "备用盘替换在设计上是临时的；在管理员处理之前，池会一直保持此状态。物理更换故障磁盘，并通过 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-replace,`zpool replace`] 对新设备完成 resilver 后，使用 `zpool detach _mypool_ _ada3p3_` 将备用盘恢复为待命状态。若要将备用盘转为 vdev 的永久成员，则使用 `zpool detach _mypool_ _ada1p3_` 分离故障设备。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1278
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `autoreplace` pool property, off by default, controls what happens when "
"a new disk appears at the same physical location as a device that previously "
"belonged to the pool.  With `autoreplace` set to `on`, ZFS replaces the old "
"device with the new disk automatically, without requiring a `zpool replace` "
"command:"
msgstr "池属性 `autoreplace` 默认关闭，用于控制当新磁盘出现在曾属于该池的设备所在的同一物理位置时的处理方式。将 `autoreplace` 设为 `on` 后，ZFS 会自动用新磁盘替换旧设备，无需执行 `zpool replace` 命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1282
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool set autoreplace=on mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool set autoreplace=on mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1287
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On FreeBSD, automatic reactions to failures, including honoring "
"`autoreplace`, are performed by man:zfsd[8], the ZFS fault management daemon "
"in the base system.  The daemon is not enabled by default.  Enable and start "
"it with:"
msgstr "在 FreeBSD 上，故障发生后的自动响应（包括遵循 `autoreplace` 设置）由 man:zfsd[8] 执行；它是基本系统中的 ZFS 故障管理守护进程。该守护进程默认未启用。使用以下命令启用并启动它："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1292
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# sysrc zfsd_enable=\"YES\"\n"
"# service zfsd start\n"
msgstr "# sysrc zfsd_enable=\"YES\"\n# service zfsd start\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1295
#, fuzzy
msgid "man:zfsd[8] listens for pool events and:"
msgstr "man:zfsd[8] 会监听池事件，并执行以下操作："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1297
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Activates a hot spare when a device disappears from a redundant vdev or when "
"a vdev becomes degraded or faulted."
msgstr "当冗余 vdev 中的设备消失，或 vdev 变为降级或故障状态时，启用热备用盘。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1298
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Marks a vdev as faulted when it produces more than 50 I/O errors or more "
"than 8 delayed I/O operations in a 60 second period, then activates a hot "
"spare."
msgstr "当 vdev 在 60 秒内产生超过 50 次 I/O 错误或超过 8 次延迟 I/O 操作时，将其标记为故障，然后启用热备盘。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1299
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Marks a vdev as degraded when it produces more than 50 checksum errors in a "
"60 second period, then activates a hot spare."
msgstr "当 vdev 在 60 秒内产生超过 50 次校验和错误时，将其标记为降级，然后启用热备盘。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1300
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Brings a device back online when it reappears, triggering a resilver of the "
"data written while it was missing."
msgstr "设备重新出现时使其恢复联机，并触发对其缺失期间写入数据的重新同步。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1301
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Replaces a missing device with a new disk that appears at the same physical "
"location when the pool has `autoreplace` set to `on`."
msgstr "当池的 `autoreplace` 设置为 `on` 时，用出现在同一物理位置的新磁盘替换缺失的设备。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1302
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Returns hot spares to standby once the resilver of a permanent replacement "
"completes."
msgstr "永久替换设备的重新同步完成后，使热备盘恢复待机状态。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1307
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD uses man:zfsd[8] for fault management.  The ZFS Event Daemon (ZED) "
"found on Linux OpenZFS platforms is not part of FreeBSD."
msgstr "FreeBSD 使用 man:zfsd[8] 进行故障管理。Linux OpenZFS 平台上的 ZFS 事件守护进程（ZED）不属于 FreeBSD。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1313
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Inspect the event stream that drives these decisions with `zpool events`.  "
"Adding `-v` shows the full payload of each event, and `-f` keeps the command "
"running, printing new events as they arrive.  ZFS also delivers these events "
"to man:devd[8].  The rules in [.filename]#/etc/devd/zfs.conf# log them to "
"the system log and serve as a template for custom actions, such as sending "
"mail when a pool becomes degraded."
msgstr "使用 `zpool events` 检查驱动这些决策的事件流。添加 `-v` 会显示每个事件的完整负载，而 `-f` 会使命令持续运行，并在新事件到达时将其打印出来。ZFS 也会将这些事件发送给 man:devd[8]。[.filename]#/etc/devd/zfs.conf# 中的规则会将它们记录到系统日志中，也可作为自定义操作的模板，例如在池降级时发送邮件。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1315
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scrubbing a Pool"
msgstr "清理存储池"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1320
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Routinely crossref:zfs[zfs-term-scrub,scrub] pools, ideally at least once "
"every month.  The `scrub` operation is disk-intensive and will reduce "
"performance while running.  Avoid high-demand periods when scheduling "
"`scrub`, or lower its impact with the I/O scheduler tunables described in "
"crossref:zfs[zfs-advanced-tuning,Tuning]."
msgstr "定期对池执行 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-scrub,清理]，最好至少每月一次。`scrub` 操作会大量占用磁盘资源，运行时会降低性能。安排 `scrub` 时应避开高负载时段，或者使用 crossref:zfs[zfs-advanced-tuning,调优] 中介绍的 I/O 调度器可调参数来降低其影响。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1331
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool scrub mypool\n"
"# zpool status\n"
"  pool: mypool\n"
" state: ONLINE\n"
"  scan: scrub in progress since Sat Jul 11 20:52:54 2026\n"
"        130G / 8.60T scanned at 649M/s, 116G / 8.60T issued at 580M/s\n"
"        0B repaired, 1.32% done, 04:15:41 to go\n"
"config:\n"
msgstr "# zpool scrub mypool\n# zpool status\n  pool: mypool\n state: ONLINE\n  scan: scrub in progress since Sat Jul 11 20:52:54 2026\n        130G / 8.60T scanned at 649M/s, 116G / 8.60T issued at 580M/s\n        0B repaired, 1.32% done, 04:15:41 to go\nconfig:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1350
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Pause a running scrub with `zpool scrub -p _mypool_` when it interferes with "
"other work; running `zpool scrub _mypool_` again resumes it from where it "
"stopped.  To cancel a scrub operation instead, run `zpool scrub -s "
"_mypool_`.  `zpool scrub -w _mypool_` waits until the scrub completes before "
"returning, which is useful in scripts.  After a scrub reports errors, `zpool "
"scrub -e _mypool_` performs an _error scrub_ that re-verifies only the "
"blocks with known errors, finishing much faster than a full scrub.  The "
"error scrub requires OpenZFS 2.2, first shipped in FreeBSD 14.0."
msgstr "当正在运行的清理操作影响其他工作时，可用 `zpool scrub -p _mypool_` 暂停它；再次运行 `zpool scrub _mypool_` 会从停止处继续。若要取消清理操作，则运行 `zpool scrub -s _mypool_`。`zpool scrub -w _mypool_` 会等待清理完成后再返回，适用于脚本。在清理报告错误后，`zpool scrub -e _mypool_` 会执行__错误清理__，仅重新验证已知有错误的块，因此比完整清理快得多。错误清理需要 OpenZFS 2.2，该版本首次随 FreeBSD 14.0 发布。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1353
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:periodic[8] can run scrubs automatically.  To scrub every pool whose "
"last scrub is more than 35 days old, add this line to [.filename]#/etc/"
"periodic.conf#:"
msgstr "man:periodic[8] 可以自动运行清理操作。若要清理上次清理时间距今超过 35 天的所有池，请将以下行添加到 [.filename]#/etc/periodic.conf#："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1357
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "daily_scrub_zfs_enable=\"YES\"\n"
msgstr "daily_status_zfs_enable=\"YES\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1362
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Set `daily_scrub_zfs_default_threshold=\"_days_\"` to change the number of "
"days between scrubs.  man:periodic.conf[5] also describes per-pool "
"thresholds.  Setting `daily_status_zfs_enable=\"YES\"` adds a pool health "
"check to the daily man:periodic[8] report."
msgstr "设置 `daily_scrub_zfs_default_threshold=\"_days_\"` 可更改两次清理之间的天数。man:periodic.conf[5] 还介绍了每个池的阈值。设置 `daily_status_zfs_enable=\"YES\"` 会在每日 man:periodic[8] 报告中添加池健康检查。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1364
#, no-wrap
msgid "Self-Healing"
msgstr "自我修复"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1375
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The checksums stored with data blocks enable the file system to _self-"
"heal_.  This feature will automatically repair data whose checksum does not "
"match the one recorded on another device that is part of the storage pool.  "
"For example, a mirror configuration with two disks where one drive is "
"starting to malfunction and cannot properly store the data any more.  This "
"is worse when the data was not accessed for a long time, as with long term "
"archive storage.  Traditional file systems need to run commands that check "
"and repair the data like man:fsck[8].  These commands take time, and in "
"severe cases, an administrator has to decide which repair operation to "
"perform.  When ZFS detects a data block with a mismatched checksum, it tries "
"to read the data from the mirror disk.  If that disk can provide the correct "
"data, ZFS will give that to the application and correct the data on the disk "
"with the wrong checksum.  This happens without any interaction from a system "
"administrator during normal pool operation."
msgstr "与数据块一同存储的校验和使文件系统能够__自我修复__。当数据的校验和与存储池中另一台设备上记录的校验和不匹配时，此功能会自动修复数据。例如，在包含两块磁盘的镜像配置中，其中一个磁盘可能开始发生故障，无法再正确存储数据。如果数据长时间未被访问，例如长期归档存储中的数据，情况会更糟。传统文件系统需要运行 man:fsck[8] 等命令来检查并修复数据。这些命令耗时较长，而且在严重情况下，管理员必须决定执行哪种修复操作。当 ZFS 检测到校验和不匹配的数据块时，会尝试从镜像磁盘读取数据。如果该磁盘能提供正确的数据，ZFS 就会将其提供给应用程序，并修正校验和错误磁盘上的数据。池正常运行期间，这一过程无需系统管理员介入。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1377
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The next example shows this self-healing behavior by creating a mirrored "
"pool of partitions [.filename]#/dev/ada0p1# and [.filename]#/dev/ada1p1#."
msgstr ""
"接下来的例子会示范自我修复会如何运作。建立一个使用磁盘 <filename>/dev/ada0</"
"filename> 及<filename>/dev/ada1</filename> 做镜像的存储池。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1385
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool create healer mirror /dev/ada0p1 /dev/ada1p1\n"
"# zpool status healer\n"
"  pool: healer\n"
" state: ONLINE\n"
"config:\n"
msgstr "# zpool create healer mirror /dev/ada0p1 /dev/ada1p1\n# zpool status healer\n  pool: healer\n state: ONLINE\nconfig:\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1391
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1545
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"    NAME        STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n"
"    healer      ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"      mirror-0  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"       ada0p1   ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"       ada1p1   ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
msgstr "    NAME        STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n    healer      ONLINE       0     0     0\n      mirror-0  ONLINE       0     0     0\n       ada0p1   ONLINE       0     0     0\n       ada1p1   ONLINE       0     0     0\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1396
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
