#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1552
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "TRIM and Initialization"
msgstr "TRIM 与初始化"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1556
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Solid state drives and thinly provisioned storage perform best when ZFS "
"tells them which blocks are no longer in use.  `zpool trim` passes that "
"information to every device in the pool that supports the TRIM or UNMAP "
"commands:"
msgstr "当 ZFS 告知固态硬盘和精简配置存储哪些数据块已不再使用时，它们的性能会更好。`zpool trim` 会将此信息传递给池中支持 TRIM 或 UNMAP 命令的每台设备："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1560
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool trim mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool trim mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1565
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Trim a single device by naming it after the pool, as in `zpool trim mypool "
"nda0p3`.  `zpool trim -w` waits until trimming completes, `-c` cancels a "
"running trim, and `-s` suspends it; running `zpool trim` again resumes a "
"suspended trim.  On devices that support it, `zpool trim --secure` requests "
"a secure TRIM, where the device guarantees erasing the data stored on the "
"trimmed blocks."
msgstr "在池名后指定设备名即可对单台设备执行 TRIM，例如 `zpool trim mypool nda0p3`。`zpool trim -w` 会等待 TRIM 完成，`-c` 会取消正在运行的 TRIM，`-s` 会暂停 TRIM；再次运行 `zpool trim` 会恢复已暂停的 TRIM。在支持此功能的设备上，`zpool trim --secure` 会请求安全 TRIM，设备会保证擦除已执行 TRIM 的数据块中存储的数据。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1567
#, fuzzy
msgid "`zpool status -t` shows the trim progress for each device:"
msgstr "`zpool status -t` 会显示每台设备的 TRIM 进度："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1575
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool status -t mypool\n"
"  pool: mypool\n"
" state: ONLINE\n"
"  scan: scrub repaired 0B in 00:12:33 with 0 errors on Sat Jul 11 03:31:11 2026\n"
"config:\n"
msgstr "# zpool status -t mypool\n  pool: mypool\n state: ONLINE\n  scan: scrub repaired 0B in 00:12:33 with 0 errors on Sat Jul 11 03:31:11 2026\nconfig:\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1581
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"    NAME        STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n"
"    mypool      ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"      mirror-0  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"        nda0p3  ONLINE       0     0     0  (23% trimmed, started at Sat Jul 11 09:15:04 2026)\n"
"        nda1p3  ONLINE       0     0     0  (22% trimmed, started at Sat Jul 11 09:15:04 2026)\n"
msgstr "    NAME        STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n    mypool      ONLINE       0     0     0\n      mirror-0  ONLINE       0     0     0\n        nda0p3  ONLINE       0     0     0  (23% trimmed, started at Sat Jul 11 09:15:04 2026)\n        nda1p3  ONLINE       0     0     0  (22% trimmed, started at Sat Jul 11 09:15:04 2026)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1586
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Setting the `autotrim` pool property to `on` makes ZFS issue small TRIM "
"commands continuously as the pool frees space:"
msgstr "将池属性 `autotrim` 设置为 `on`，可使 ZFS 在池释放空间时持续发出小型 TRIM 命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1590
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool set autotrim=on mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool set autotrim=on mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1595
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Automatic trimming skips small freed regions and puts a constant extra load "
"on the devices.  For most systems, leaving `autotrim` off and running a full "
"`zpool trim` on a schedule gives better results.  On FreeBSD 14.1 and later, "
"man:periodic[8] runs such a trim daily when [.filename]#/etc/periodic.conf# "
"contains `daily_trim_zfs_enable=\"YES\"`."
msgstr "自动 TRIM 会跳过较小的已释放区域，并持续给设备增加额外负载。对于大多数系统，关闭 `autotrim` 并按计划运行完整的 `zpool trim` 效果更好。在 FreeBSD 14.1 及更高版本中，如果 [.filename]#/etc/periodic.conf# 包含 `daily_trim_zfs_enable=\"YES\"`，man:periodic[8] 会每天运行此类 TRIM。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1598
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`zpool initialize` is the counterpart of trimming: it writes a pattern to "
"all unallocated space on the specified devices, or on every eligible device "
"in the pool when given no device names.  This forces the backing storage to "
"allocate the space up front, avoiding first-write latency on thinly "
"provisioned virtual disks, and exercises new devices before trusting them "
"with data."
msgstr "`zpool initialize` 是 TRIM 的对应操作：它会向指定设备的所有未分配空间写入一种模式；如果未指定设备名，则会对池中每台符合条件的设备执行此操作。这会迫使底层存储预先分配空间，避免精简配置虚拟磁盘首次写入时的延迟，并可在信任新设备来存储数据之前对其进行测试。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1602
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool initialize mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool initialize mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1606
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"As with trimming, `-c` cancels an initialization, `-s` suspends it, and `-w` "
"waits for it to finish; `-u` removes the initialization state from the "
"devices.  See man:zpool-trim[8] and man:zpool-initialize[8] for details."
msgstr "与 TRIM 一样，`-c` 会取消初始化，`-s` 会暂停初始化，`-w` 会等待其完成；`-u` 会从设备中移除初始化状态。详情请参见 man:zpool-trim[8] 和 man:zpool-initialize[8]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1608
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Pool Checkpoints"
msgstr "池检查点"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1612
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`zpool checkpoint` saves the state of the entire pool, including every "
"dataset and the pool configuration, so that a later rewind returns the pool "
"to the exact state it had when creating the checkpoint.  Create a checkpoint "
"before risky administrative operations such as upgrading the operating "
"system, enabling new pool features, or reorganizing datasets:"
msgstr "`zpool checkpoint` 会保存整个池的状态，包括每个数据集和池配置，以便稍后回滚时将池恢复到创建检查点时的确切状态。在执行升级操作系统、启用新的池功能或重新组织数据集等有风险的管理操作前，请创建检查点："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1616
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool checkpoint mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool checkpoint mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1620
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A pool holds at most one checkpoint at a time.  The `CKPOINT` column of "
"`zpool list` shows how much space the checkpoint consumes as the pool "
"diverges from the saved state:"
msgstr "一个池一次最多只能有一个检查点。随着池状态偏离已保存状态，`zpool list` 的 `CKPOINT` 列会显示检查点占用的空间："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1626
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool list mypool\n"
"NAME     SIZE  ALLOC   FREE  CKPOINT  EXPANDSZ   FRAG    CAP  DEDUP    HEALTH  ALTROOT\n"
"mypool  4.50T  1.42T  3.08T     221M         -     4%    31%  1.00x    ONLINE  -\n"
msgstr "# zpool list mypool\nNAME     SIZE  ALLOC   FREE  CKPOINT  EXPANDSZ   FRAG    CAP  DEDUP    HEALTH  ALTROOT\nmypool  4.50T  1.42T  3.08T     221M         -     4%    31%  1.00x    ONLINE  -\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1629
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To rewind, export the pool and import it again with `--rewind-to-checkpoint`:"
msgstr "要回滚，请先导出池，然后使用 `--rewind-to-checkpoint` 再次导入："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1634
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool export mypool\n"
"# zpool import --rewind-to-checkpoint mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool export mypool\n# zpool import --rewind-to-checkpoint mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1638
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Rewinding discards every change made to the pool after creating the "
"checkpoint, including newer snapshots and property changes.  Discard a "
"checkpoint that is no longer needed to release the space it holds; `-w` "
"waits until the discard completes:"
msgstr "回滚会丢弃创建检查点后对池所做的所有更改，包括较新的快照和属性更改。丢弃不再需要的检查点以释放其占用的空间；`-w` 会等待丢弃操作完成："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1642
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool checkpoint -d -w mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool checkpoint -d -w mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1646
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"While a checkpoint exists, ZFS refuses operations that change the pool "
"structure: `zpool remove`, `zpool attach`, `zpool detach`, `zpool split`, "
"and `zpool reguid`.  Space freed after creating the checkpoint is not "
"reclaimed until the checkpoint is discarded, so a long-lived checkpoint on a "
"busy pool can fill it up."
msgstr "检查点存在期间，ZFS 会拒绝更改池结构的操作：`zpool remove`、`zpool attach`、`zpool detach`、`zpool split` 和 `zpool reguid`。创建检查点后释放的空间只有在检查点被丢弃后才会回收，因此，在繁忙的池中长期保留检查点可能会导致池空间耗尽。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1651
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A checkpoint is not a replacement for crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot,"
"snapshots] or backups.  It protects against administrative mistakes for a "
"short period, lives on the same disks as the pool, and rewinding discards "
"everything written after its creation."
msgstr "检查点不能替代 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot,快照] 或备份。它只能在短时间内防止管理操作失误，存储在池所在的同一组磁盘上，而且回滚会丢弃创建检查点后写入的所有内容。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1654
#, fuzzy
msgid "See man:zpool-checkpoint[8] for details."
msgstr "详情请参见 man:zpool-checkpoint[8]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1656
#, no-wrap
msgid "Growing a Pool"
msgstr "扩增存储池"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1666
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The smallest device in each vdev limits the usable size of a redundant "
"pool.  Replace the smallest device with a larger device.  After completing a "
"crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-replace,replace] or crossref:zfs[zfs-term-resilver,"
"resilver] operation, the pool can grow to use the capacity of the new "
"device.  For example, consider a mirror of a 1 TB drive and a 2 TB drive.  "
"The usable space is 1 TB.  When replacing the 1 TB drive with another 2 TB "
"drive, the resilvering process copies the existing data onto the new drive.  "
"As both of the devices now have 2 TB capacity, the mirror's available space "
"grows to 2 TB."
msgstr ""
"可用的备援存储池大小会受到每个 vdev 中容量最小的设备限制。最小的设备可以替换"
"成较大的设备，在更换（<link linkend=\"zfs-zpool-replace\">Replace</link>）或"
"修复（<link linkend=\"zfs-term-resilver\">Resilver</link>）作业后，存储池可以"
"成长到该新设备的可用容量。例如，要做一个 1 TB 磁盘机与一个 2 TB 磁盘机的镜"
"像，可用的空间会是1 TB，当1 TB 磁盘机备更换成另一个 2 TB 的磁盘机时，修复程序"
"会复制既有的资料到新的磁盘机，由于现在两个设备都有 2 TB 的容量，所以镜像的可"
"用空间便会成长到 2 TB。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1669
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The pool does not use the new capacity automatically by default.  Set the "
"`autoexpand` pool property to `on` before replacing the devices and the pool "
"grows as soon as the last smaller device leaves the vdev:"
msgstr "默认情况下，池不会自动使用新增容量。在替换设备前，将池属性 `autoexpand` 设置为 `on`，最后一台较小的设备从 vdev 中移除后，池便会扩容："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1673
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool set autoexpand=on mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool set autoexpand=on mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1677
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Otherwise, start expansion by using `zpool online -e` on each device.  After "
"expanding all devices, the extra space becomes available to the pool."
msgstr "否则，可对每台设备使用 `zpool online -e` 来启动扩容。所有设备扩容后，额外空间便可供池使用。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1679
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To grow a RAID-Z vdev by adding a disk instead of replacing the existing "
"ones, see crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-raidz-expansion,RAID-Z Expansion]."
msgstr "若要通过添加磁盘而非替换现有磁盘来扩展 RAID-Z vdev，请参见 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-raidz-expansion,RAID-Z 扩展]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1681
#, no-wrap
msgid "Importing and Exporting Pools"
msgstr "导入与导出存储池"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1689
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"_Export_ pools before moving them to another system.  ZFS unmounts all "
"datasets, marking each device as exported but still locked to prevent use by "
"other disks.  This allows pools to be _imported_ on other machines, other "
"operating systems that support ZFS, and even different hardware "
"architectures (with some caveats, see man:zpool[8]).  When a dataset has "
"open files, use `zpool export -f` to force exporting the pool.  Use this "
"with caution.  The datasets are forcibly unmounted, potentially resulting in "
"unexpected behavior by the applications which had open files on those "
"datasets."
msgstr "将池移至另一台系统前，请先__导出__池。ZFS 会卸载所有数据集，将每台设备标记为已导出，但仍会锁定设备以防其他磁盘使用。这样便可在其他计算机、支持 ZFS 的其他操作系统，甚至不同的硬件架构上__导入__池（有一些注意事项，参见 man:zpool[8]）。如果数据集中存在打开的文件，可使用 `zpool export -f` 强制导出池。请谨慎使用此命令。数据集会被强制卸载，可能导致正在使用这些数据集中打开文件的应用程序出现意外行为。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1691
msgid "Export a pool that is not in use:"
msgstr "导出未使用的存储池："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1695
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool export mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool export mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1703
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Importing a pool automatically mounts the datasets.  If this is undesired "
"behavior, use `zpool import -N` to prevent it.  `zpool import -o` sets "
"temporary properties for this specific import.  `zpool import -o altroot=` "
"allows importing a pool with a base mount point instead of the root of the "
"file system.  If the pool was last used on a different system and was not "
"properly exported, force the import using `zpool import -f`.  `zpool import -"
"a` imports all pools that do not appear to be in use by another system."
msgstr ""
"导入存储池会自动挂载数据集，若不想自动挂载，可以使用 <command>zpool import -"
"N</command>。<command>zpool import -o</command> 可以设定在导入时暂时使用的属"
"性。<command>zpool import altroot=</command> 允许导入时指定基础挂载点（Base "
"mount point）来替换文件系统根目录。若存储池先前用在不同的系统且不正常导出，可"
"能会需要使用 <command>zpool import -f</command> 来强制导入。<command>zpool "
"import -a</command> 会导入所有没有被其他系统使用的存储池。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1709
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:zpool-import[8] also provides options for recovering damaged pools.  "
"`zpool import -F` attempts to rewind the pool to an earlier transaction "
"group when the most recent ones are damaged, discarding the last few seconds "
"of writes.  `zpool import -m` allows importing a pool whose dedicated log "
"device is missing.  `zpool import -o readonly=on` imports the pool read-"
"only, preventing all writes, which is useful for forensics or when rescuing "
"data from a failing pool.  `zpool import -R /mnt` combines `altroot=/mnt` "
"with `cachefile=none`, keeping a rescue import from disturbing the mount "
"paths and the pool cache of the running system."
msgstr "man:zpool-import[8] 还提供了恢复受损存储池的选项。`zpool import -F` 会在最近的事务组受损时尝试将存储池回退到较早的事务组，并丢弃最后几秒内的写入。`zpool import -m` 可导入缺少专用日志设备的存储池。`zpool import -o readonly=on` 以只读方式导入存储池，禁止所有写入，适用于取证或从故障存储池中抢救数据。`zpool import -R /mnt` 将 `altroot=/mnt` 与 `cachefile=none` 结合使用，避免救援导入影响正在运行的系统的挂载路径和存储池缓存。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1711
msgid "List all available pools for import:"
msgstr "列出所有可导入的存储池："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1720
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool import\n"
"   pool: mypool\n"
"     id: 9930174748043525076\n"
"  state: ONLINE\n"
" action: The pool can be imported using its name or numeric identifier.\n"
" config:\n"
msgstr "# zpool import\n   pool: mypool\n     id: 9930174748043525076\n  state: ONLINE\n action: The pool can be imported using its name or numeric identifier.\n config:\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1723
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"        mypool    ONLINE\n"
"          ada0p1  ONLINE\n"
msgstr "        mypool    ONLINE\n          ada0p1  ONLINE\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1726
msgid "Import the pool with an alternative root directory:"
msgstr "使用替代的根目录导入存储池："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1733
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool import -o altroot=/mnt mypool\n"
"# zfs list\n"
"NAME                 USED  AVAIL  REFER  MOUNTPOINT\n"
"mypool               110K  47.0G    31K  /mnt/mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool import -o altroot=/mnt mypool\n# zfs list\nNAME                 USED  AVAIL  REFER  MOUNTPOINT\nmypool               110K  47.0G    31K  /mnt/mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1738
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"At boot, the ZFS startup scripts enabled by `zfs_enable=\"YES\"` in [."
"filename]#/etc/rc.conf# import every pool recorded in [.filename]#/etc/zfs/"
"zpool.cache#.  Importing a pool adds it to that cache file automatically; "
"the `cachefile` pool property controls this behavior.  Pools imported with "
"`cachefile=none` do not come back automatically after a reboot."
msgstr "启动时，由 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中的 `zfs_enable=\"YES\"` 启用的 ZFS 启动脚本会导入 [.filename]#/etc/zfs/zpool.cache# 中记录的每个存储池。导入存储池会自动将其添加到该缓存文件；存储池属性 `cachefile` 控制此行为。使用 `cachefile=none` 导入的存储池在重启后不会自动恢复。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1740
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Importing and Exporting Pools"
msgid "Importing a GELI-Encrypted Pool"
msgstr "导入与导出存储池"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1744
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `Encrypt Disks` option of the FreeBSD installer encrypts the pool's "
"partitions with man:geli[8], described in crossref:disks[disks-encrypting-"
"geli,\"Encrypting Disk Partitions\"], rather than with crossref:zfs[zfs-"
"native-encryption,ZFS native encryption].  On the installed system the "
"loader prompts for the passphrase and attaches the providers before mounting "
"the root pool, but ZFS itself knows nothing about the encryption: when "
"booting from rescue media or moving the disks to another host, `zpool "
"import` does not find the pool until the GELI providers are attached."
msgstr "FreeBSD 安装程序中的 `Encrypt Disks` 选项使用 man:geli[8] 加密存储池的分区，相关说明见 crossref:disks[disks-encrypting-geli,\"加密磁盘分区\"]，而不是使用 crossref:zfs[zfs-native-encryption,ZFS 原生加密]。在已安装的系统上，loader 会提示输入密码短语，并在挂载根存储池之前附加提供者，但 ZFS 本身并不知道加密的存在：从救援介质启动或将磁盘移至另一台主机时，必须先附加 GELI 提供者，`zpool import` 才能找到该存储池。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1746
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Attach the encrypted [.filename]#freebsd-zfs# partition of every disk in the "
"pool, supplying the passphrase, then import the pool:"
msgstr "附加存储池中每个磁盘上已加密的 [.filename]#freebsd-zfs# 分区，并输入密码短语，然后导入存储池："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1752
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# geli attach ada0p4\n"
"Enter passphrase:\n"
"# zpool import -f -R /mnt zroot\n"
msgstr "# geli attach ada0p4\nEnter passphrase:\n# zpool import -f -R /mnt zroot\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1756
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Use `gpart show` to identify the [.filename]#freebsd-zfs# partitions; with "
"the default installer layout the encrypted partition is [.filename]#p4#.  "
"Systems installed with the legacy layout, which keeps a separate unencrypted "
"boot pool, additionally store a key file in [.filename]#/boot/encryption."
"key# on that pool; attach those providers with `geli attach -k /path/to/"
"encryption.key`."
msgstr "使用 `gpart show` 查找 [.filename]#freebsd-zfs# 分区；在安装程序的默认布局中，加密分区为 [.filename]#p4#。使用旧式布局安装的系统会保留一个单独的未加密启动存储池，并在该存储池的 [.filename]#/boot/encryption.key# 中存储密钥文件；使用 `geli attach -k /path/to/encryption.key` 附加这些提供者。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1758
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upgrading a Storage Pool"
msgstr "升级存储池"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1764
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"After upgrading FreeBSD, or if importing a pool from a system using an older "
"version, manually upgrade the pool to make new on-disk features available.  "
"Consider whether the pool may ever need importing on an older system before "
"upgrading.  Upgrading is a one-way process.  Upgrading older pools is "
"possible, but downgrading pools with newer features is not."
msgstr ""
"在升级 FreeBSD 之后或存储池是由其他使用旧版 <acronym>ZFS</acronym> 的系统汇"
"入，存储池可以手动升级到最新版本的 <acronym>ZFS</acronym> 来支持新的功能。在"
"升级前请评估存储池是否还要在旧的系统做汇入，由于升级是一个单向的程序，旧的存"
"储池可以升级，但有新功能的存储池无法降级。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1770
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Pools do not carry a single version number anymore.  Instead, each on-disk "
"format change is an individual _feature flag_, described in man:zpool-"
"features[7].  A feature is _enabled_ when the pool allows its use and "
"becomes _active_ once the pool stores data that depends on it.  An enabled "
"but inactive feature does not affect compatibility.  Once a feature is "
"active, software without support for it can no longer import the pool, "
"although pools whose active features are all \"read-only compatible\" still "
"allow read-only imports."
msgstr "存储池不再使用单一版本号，而是将每项磁盘格式变更作为单独的__功能标志__，详见 man:zpool-features[7]。当存储池允许使用某项功能时，该功能处于__启用__状态；存储池一旦存储了依赖该功能的数据，该功能便会变为__活动__状态。已启用但未活动的功能不会影响兼容性。功能一旦处于活动状态，不支持它的软件便无法再导入该存储池；不过，如果所有活动功能都“只读兼容”，仍可只读导入存储池。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1772
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`zpool status` reports when supported features are not enabled on a pool:"
msgstr "当存储池上有受支持的功能尚未启用时，`zpool status` 会报告此情况："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1785
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool status mypool\n"
"  pool: mypool\n"
" state: ONLINE\n"
"status: Some supported and requested features are not enabled on the pool.\n"
"        The pool can still be used, but some features are unavailable.\n"
"action: Enable all features using 'zpool upgrade'. Once this is done,\n"
"        the pool may no longer be accessible by software that does not support\n"
"        the features. See zpool-features(7) for details.\n"
"  scan: scrub repaired 0B in 00:11:03 with 0 errors on Sat Jul 11 03:15:41 2026\n"
"config:\n"
msgstr "# zpool status mypool\n  pool: mypool\n state: ONLINE\nstatus: Some supported and requested features are not enabled on the pool.\n        The pool can still be used, but some features are unavailable.\naction: Enable all features using 'zpool upgrade'. Once this is done,\n        the pool may no longer be accessible by software that does not support\n        the features. See zpool-features(7) for details.\n  scan: scrub repaired 0B in 00:11:03 with 0 errors on Sat Jul 11 03:15:41 2026\nconfig:\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1791
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"        NAME        STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n"
"        mypool      ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"          mirror-0  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            ada0p1  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
"            ada1p1  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"
msgstr "        NAME        STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n        mypool      ONLINE       0     0     0\n          mirror-0  ONLINE       0     0     0\n            ada0p1  ONLINE       0     0     0\n            ada1p1  ONLINE       0     0     0\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1796
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Running `zpool upgrade` without arguments lists every pool with disabled "
"features:"
msgstr "不带参数运行 `zpool upgrade` 会列出所有具有未启用功能的存储池："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1801
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool upgrade\n"
"This system supports ZFS pool feature flags.\n"
msgstr "# zpool upgrade\nThis system supports ZFS pool feature flags.\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1805
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Some supported features are not enabled on the following pools. Once a\n"
"feature is enabled the pool may become incompatible with software\n"
"that does not support the feature. See zpool-features(7) for details.\n"
msgstr "Some supported features are not enabled on the following pools. Once a\nfeature is enabled the pool may become incompatible with software\nthat does not support the feature. See zpool-features(7) for details.\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1808
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Note that the pool 'compatibility' feature can be used to inhibit\n"
"feature upgrades.\n"
msgstr "Note that the pool 'compatibility' feature can be used to inhibit\nfeature upgrades.\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1817
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"POOL  FEATURE\n"
"---------------\n"
"mypool\n"
"      zilsaxattr\n"
"      head_errlog\n"
"      blake3\n"
"      block_cloning\n"
"      vdev_zaps_v2\n"
msgstr "POOL  FEATURE\n---------------\nmypool\n      zilsaxattr\n      head_errlog\n      blake3\n      block_cloning\n      vdev_zaps_v2\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1821
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Use `zpool upgrade -v` to list every feature the running system supports, "
"together with the legacy version numbers.  Enable all supported features on "
"a pool:"
msgstr "使用 `zpool upgrade -v` 列出正在运行的系统所支持的所有功能及其旧版版本号。启用存储池支持的所有功能："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1826
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Upgrade a pool to support additional feature flags:"
msgid ""
"# zpool upgrade mypool\n"
"This system supports ZFS pool feature flags.\n"
msgstr "升级存储池支持新版的功能旗标（Feature flags）："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1833
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Enabled the following features on 'mypool':\n"
"  zilsaxattr\n"
"  head_errlog\n"
"  blake3\n"
"  block_cloning\n"
"  vdev_zaps_v2\n"
msgstr "Enabled the following features on 'mypool':\n  zilsaxattr\n  head_errlog\n  blake3\n  block_cloning\n  vdev_zaps_v2\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1836
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Pools that must stay importable on systems running older ZFS software can "
"restrict which features `zpool create` and `zpool upgrade` enable through "
"the `compatibility` pool property:"
msgstr "如果存储池必须能在运行较旧 ZFS 软件的系统上导入，可以通过 `compatibility` 存储池属性限制 `zpool create` 和 `zpool upgrade` 启用的功能："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1840
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool create -o compatibility=openzfs-2.1-freebsd mypool mirror /dev/ada0p1 /dev/ada1p1\n"
msgstr "# zpool create -o compatibility=openzfs-2.1-freebsd mypool mirror /dev/ada0p1 /dev/ada1p1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1845
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Setting the property on an existing pool with `zpool set` works as well.  "
"Each named feature set corresponds to a file in [.filename]#/usr/share/zfs/"
"compatibility.d#, and the default value `off` allows every feature.  Setting "
"the property does not disable features that are already enabled."
msgstr "也可以使用 `zpool set` 为现有存储池设置此属性。每个命名的功能集都对应 [.filename]#/usr/share/zfs/compatibility.d# 中的一个文件；默认值 `off` 允许使用所有功能。设置此属性不会禁用已启用的功能。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1851
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Update the boot code on systems that boot from a pool to support the new "
"pool features.  Use `gpart bootcode` on the partition that contains the boot "
"code.  Two types of bootcode are available, depending on the way the system "
"boots: GPT (the most common option) and EFI (for more modern systems)."
msgstr "对于从存储池启动的系统，请更新启动代码以支持新的存储池功能。使用 `gpart bootcode` 更新包含启动代码的分区。根据系统的启动方式，有两种类型的启动代码可用：GPT（最常见的选项）和 EFI（适用于较新的系统）。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1853
msgid "For legacy boot using GPT, use the following command:"
msgstr "对使用GPT分区的boot，使用以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1857
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# gpart bootcode -b /boot/pmbr -p /boot/gptzfsboot -i 1 ada1\n"
msgstr "# gpart bootcode -b /boot/pmbr -p /boot/gptzfsboot -i 1 ada1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1860
msgid "For systems using EFI to boot, execute the following command:"
msgstr "对使用EFI的启动方式，请执行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1866
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# mount -t msdosfs /dev/ada1p1 /boot/efi\n"
"# cp /boot/loader.efi /boot/efi/efi/boot/BOOTX64.efi\n"
"# cp /boot/loader.efi /boot/efi/efi/freebsd/loader.efi\n"
msgstr "# mount -t msdosfs /dev/ada1p1 /boot/efi\n# cp /boot/loader.efi /boot/efi/efi/boot/BOOTX64.efi\n# cp /boot/loader.efi /boot/efi/efi/freebsd/loader.efi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1871
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"These instructions apply to amd64 systems.  Depending on the architecture, "
"the file has a different name.  Refer to man:uefi[8] to find the names of "
"the architecture-specific files."
msgstr "这些说明适用于 amd64 系统。具体文件名因架构而异。请参阅 man:uefi[8]，了解各架构对应的文件名。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1874
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Apply the bootcode to all bootable disks in the pool.  See man:gpart[8] for "
"more information."
msgstr "对存储池中所有可启动的磁盘应用启动代码。更多信息请参阅 man:gpart[8]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1877
#, no-wrap
msgid "Displaying Recorded Pool History"
msgstr "显示已记录的存储池历史日志"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1883
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"ZFS records commands that change the pool, including creating datasets, "
"changing properties, or replacing a disk.  Reviewing history about a pool's "
"creation is useful, as is checking which user performed a specific action "
"and when.  History is not kept in a log file, but is part of the pool "
"itself.  The command to review this history is aptly named `zpool history`:"
msgstr ""
"修改存储池的指令会被记录下来，会记录的动作包含数据集的建立，属性更改或更换磁"
"盘。这个历史记录用来查看存储池是如何建立、由谁执行、什么动作及何时。历史记录"
"并非储存在日志档（Log file），而是储存在存储池。查看这个历史记录的指令名称为 "
"<command>zpool history</command>："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1892
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool history\n"
"History for 'tank':\n"
"2026-07-11.10:24:05 zpool create tank mirror /dev/ada0p1 /dev/ada1p1\n"
"2026-07-11.18:50:58 zfs set atime=off tank\n"
"2026-07-11.18:51:09 zfs set checksum=fletcher4 tank\n"
"2026-07-11.18:51:18 zfs create tank/backup\n"
msgstr "# zpool history\nHistory for 'tank':\n2026-07-11.10:24:05 zpool create tank mirror /dev/ada0p1 /dev/ada1p1\n2026-07-11.18:50:58 zfs set atime=off tank\n2026-07-11.18:51:09 zfs set checksum=fletcher4 tank\n2026-07-11.18:51:18 zfs create tank/backup\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1897
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The output shows `zpool` and `zfs` commands altering the pool in some way "
"along with a timestamp.  Commands like `zfs list` are not included.  When "
"specifying no pool name, ZFS displays history of all pools."
msgstr ""
"输出结果显示曾在该存储池上执行的 <command>zpool</command> 与 <command>zfs</"
"command> 指令以及时间戳记。只有会修改存储池或类似的指令会被记录下来，像是 "
"<command>zfs list</command> 这种指令并不会被记录。当不指定存储池名称时，会列"
"出所有存储池的历史记录。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1900
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`zpool history` can show even more information when providing the options `-"
"i` or `-l`.  `-i` displays user-initiated events as well as internally "
"logged ZFS events."
msgstr "使用 `-i` 或 `-l` 选项时，`zpool history` 可以显示更多信息。`-i` 会显示用户发起的事件以及 ZFS 内部记录的事件。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1912
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool history -i\n"
"History for 'tank':\n"
"2026-07-11.10:24:05 [txg:5] create pool version 5000; software version zfs-2.2.7-FreeBSD_gd75f9ee8b; uts myzfsbox 14.3-RELEASE 1403000 amd64\n"
"2026-07-11.18:50:53 [txg:50] set tank (21) atime=0\n"
"2026-07-11.18:50:58 zfs set atime=off tank\n"
"2026-07-11.18:51:04 [txg:53] set tank (21) checksum=7\n"
"2026-07-11.18:51:09 zfs set checksum=fletcher4 tank\n"
"2026-07-11.18:51:13 [txg:55] create tank/backup (39)\n"
"2026-07-11.18:51:18 zfs create tank/backup\n"
msgstr "# zpool history -i\nHistory for 'tank':\n2026-07-11.10:24:05 [txg:5] create pool version 5000; software version zfs-2.2.7-FreeBSD_gd75f9ee8b; uts myzfsbox 14.3-RELEASE 1403000 amd64\n2026-07-11.18:50:53 [txg:50] set tank (21) atime=0\n2026-07-11.18:50:58 zfs set atime=off tank\n2026-07-11.18:51:04 [txg:53] set tank (21) checksum=7\n2026-07-11.18:51:09 zfs set checksum=fletcher4 tank\n2026-07-11.18:51:13 [txg:55] create tank/backup (39)\n2026-07-11.18:51:18 zfs create tank/backup\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1916
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Show more details by adding `-l`.  Showing history records in a long format, "
"including information like the name of the user who issued the command and "
"the hostname on which the change happened."
msgstr ""
"更多详细的资讯可加上 <option>-l</option> 来取得，历史记录会以较长的格式显示，"
"包含的资讯有执行指令的使用者名称、主机名称以及更改的项目。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1925
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool history -l\n"
"History for 'tank':\n"
"2026-07-11.10:24:05 zpool create tank mirror /dev/ada0p1 /dev/ada1p1 [user 0 (root) on myzfsbox:global]\n"
"2026-07-11.18:50:58 zfs set atime=off tank [user 0 (root) on myzfsbox:global]\n"
"2026-07-11.18:51:09 zfs set checksum=fletcher4 tank [user 0 (root) on myzfsbox:global]\n"
"2026-07-11.18:51:18 zfs create tank/backup [user 0 (root) on myzfsbox:global]\n"
msgstr "# zpool history -l\nHistory for 'tank':\n2026-07-11.10:24:05 zpool create tank mirror /dev/ada0p1 /dev/ada1p1 [user 0 (root) on myzfsbox:global]\n2026-07-11.18:50:58 zfs set atime=off tank [user 0 (root) on myzfsbox:global]\n2026-07-11.18:51:09 zfs set checksum=fletcher4 tank [user 0 (root) on myzfsbox:global]\n2026-07-11.18:51:18 zfs create tank/backup [user 0 (root) on myzfsbox:global]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1931
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The output shows that the `root` user created the mirrored pool with disks [."
"filename]#/dev/ada0p1# and [.filename]#/dev/ada1p1#.  The hostname "
"`myzfsbox` is also shown with each command.  The hostname display becomes "
"important when exporting the pool from one system and importing on another.  "
"It's possible to distinguish the commands issued on the other system by the "
"hostname recorded for each command."
msgstr "输出显示，`root` 用户使用磁盘 [.filename]#/dev/ada0p1# 和 [.filename]#/dev/ada1p1# 创建了镜像存储池。每条命令旁也会显示主机名 `myzfsbox`。从一台系统导出存储池并在另一台系统上导入时，显示主机名就很有用。可以根据每条命令记录的主机名区分在另一台系统上执行的命令。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1934
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Combine both options to `zpool history` to give the most detailed "
"information possible for any given pool.  Pool history provides valuable "
"information when tracking down the actions performed or when needing more "
"detailed output for debugging."
msgstr ""
"两个 <command>zpool history</command> 选项可以合并使用来取得最完整的存储池详"
"细资讯。存储池历史记录在追踪执行什么动作或要取得除错所需的输出结果提供了非常"
"有用的资讯。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1936
#, no-wrap
msgid "Performance Monitoring"
msgstr "性能监控"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1943
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A built-in monitoring system can display pool I/O statistics in real time.  "
"It shows the amount of free and used space on the pool, read and write "
"operations performed per second, and I/O bandwidth used.  By default, ZFS "
"monitors and displays all pools in the system.  Provide a pool name to limit "
"monitoring to that pool.  A basic example:"
msgstr ""
"内建的监视系统可以即时显示存储池的 <acronym>I/O</acronym> 统计资讯。它会显示"
"存储池剩余的空间与使用的空间，每秒执行了多少读取与写入的操作，有多少 "
"<acronym>I/O</acronym> 带宽被使用。预设会监视所有在系统中的存储池都并显示出"
"来，可以提供存储池名称来只显示该存储池的监视资讯。举一个简单的例子："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1951
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool iostat\n"
"               capacity     operations    bandwidth\n"
"pool        alloc   free   read  write   read  write\n"
"----------  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----\n"
"data         288G  1.53T      2     11  11.3K  57.1K\n"
msgstr "# zpool iostat\n               capacity     operations    bandwidth\npool        alloc   free   read  write   read  write\n----------  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----\ndata         288G  1.53T      2     11  11.3K  57.1K\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1957
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To continuously see I/O activity, specify a number as the last parameter, "
"indicating an interval in seconds to wait between updates.  The next "
"statistic line prints after each interval.  Press kbd:[Ctrl+C] to stop this "
"continuous monitoring.  Give a second number on the command line after the "
"interval to specify the total number of statistics to display."
msgstr "要持续查看 I/O 活动，请将一个数字作为最后一个参数指定，表示两次更新之间等待的秒数。每过一个间隔就会打印一行新的统计信息。按 kbd:[Ctrl+C] 停止持续监控。在命令行的间隔参数之后再给出一个数字，可以指定要显示的统计信息总数。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1962
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Display even more detailed I/O statistics with `-v`.  Each device in the "
"pool appears with a statistics line.  This is useful for seeing read and "
"write operations performed on each device, and can help determine if any "
"individual device is slowing down the pool.  This example shows a mirrored "
"pool with two devices:"
msgstr ""
"使用 <option>-v</option> 可以显示更详细的 <acronym>I/O</acronym> 统计资讯。每"
"个在存储池中的设备会以一行统计资讯显示。这可以帮助了解每一个设备做了多少读取"
"与写入的操作，并可协助确认是否有各别设备拖慢了整个存储池的速度。以下范例会显"
"示有两个设备的镜像存储池："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1974
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool iostat -v\n"
"                            capacity     operations    bandwidth\n"
"pool                     alloc   free   read  write   read  write\n"
"-----------------------  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----\n"
"data                      288G  1.53T      2     12  9.23K  61.5K\n"
"  mirror                  288G  1.53T      2     12  9.23K  61.5K\n"
"    ada1p1                   -      -      0      4  5.61K  61.7K\n"
"    ada2p1                   -      -      1      4  5.04K  61.7K\n"
"-----------------------  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----\n"
msgstr "# zpool iostat -v\n                            capacity     operations    bandwidth\npool                     alloc   free   read  write   read  write\n-----------------------  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----\ndata                      288G  1.53T      2     12  9.23K  61.5K\n  mirror                  288G  1.53T      2     12  9.23K  61.5K\n    ada1p1                   -      -      0      4  5.61K  61.7K\n    ada2p1                   -      -      1      4  5.04K  61.7K\n-----------------------  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1980
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`zpool iostat` offers several deeper views of the I/O pipeline.  `-l` adds "
"average latency columns, splitting the total wait time into disk time and "
"time spent in the various I/O queues.  `-q` shows the number of pending and "
"active operations in each per-vdev queue.  `-w` prints full latency "
"histograms, and `-r` prints request size histograms for each leaf vdev."
msgstr "`zpool iostat` 提供了多个更深入查看 I/O 流水线的视图。`-l` 会增加平均延迟列，将总等待时间拆分为磁盘耗时和各类 I/O 队列中的等待时间。`-q` 显示每个 vdev 队列中待处理和正在处理的操作数量。`-w` 输出完整的延迟直方图，`-r` 则输出每个叶 vdev 的请求大小直方图。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1982
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The latency columns of `-l` make it easy to spot a single slow disk dragging "
"down a whole vdev:"
msgstr "`-l` 的延迟列便于发现拖慢整个 vdev 的单个慢速磁盘："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1994
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zpool iostat -lv data\n"
"              capacity     operations     bandwidth    total_wait     disk_wait    syncq_wait    asyncq_wait  scrub   trim  rebuild\n"
"pool        alloc   free   read  write   read  write   read  write   read  write   read  write   read  write   wait   wait     wait\n"
"----------  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -------\n"
"data         288G  1.53T    156    212  19.4M  26.6M   14ms  186ms    5ms  184ms    1us    2us    8ms    2ms      -      -        -\n"
"  mirror-0   288G  1.53T    156    212  19.4M  26.6M   14ms  186ms    5ms  184ms    1us    2us    8ms    2ms      -      -        -\n"
"    ada1p1      -      -     79    106   9.7M  13.3M    3ms    5ms    3ms    4ms    1us    2us    1ms    1ms      -      -        -\n"
"    ada2p1      -      -     77    106   9.7M  13.3M  212ms  187ms  208ms  183ms    1us    2us   15ms    3ms      -      -        -\n"
"----------  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -------\n"
msgstr "# zpool iostat -lv data\n              capacity     operations     bandwidth    total_wait     disk_wait    syncq_wait    asyncq_wait  scrub   trim  rebuild\npool        alloc   free   read  write   read  write   read  write   read  write   read  write   read  write   wait   wait     wait\n----------  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -------\ndata         288G  1.53T    156    212  19.4M  26.6M   14ms  186ms    5ms  184ms    1us    2us    8ms    2ms      -      -        -\n  mirror-0   288G  1.53T    156    212  19.4M  26.6M   14ms  186ms    5ms  184ms    1us    2us    8ms    2ms      -      -        -\n    ada1p1      -      -     79    106   9.7M  13.3M    3ms    5ms    3ms    4ms    1us    2us    1ms    1ms      -      -        -\n    ada2p1      -      -     77    106   9.7M  13.3M  212ms  187ms  208ms  183ms    1us    2us   15ms    3ms      -      -        -\n----------  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -----  -------\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:1999
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In this example, [.filename]#ada2p1# needs hundreds of milliseconds of disk "
"time for I/O that its mirror partner [.filename]#ada1p1# completes in single-"
"digit milliseconds, while both handle a similar number of operations.  A "
"write to the mirror only completes when the slowest member finishes, so the "
"write latency of the whole vdev tracks [.filename]#ada2p1#.  High latency at "
"normal operation counts, without read, write, or checksum errors in `zpool "
"status`, often indicates a disk that retries internally and is a candidate "
"for replacement."
msgstr "在此示例中，[.filename]#ada2p1# 完成 I/O 需要数百毫秒的磁盘时间，而其镜像伙伴 [.filename]#ada1p1# 只需个位数毫秒；两者处理的操作数量却相近。只有最慢的成员完成后，镜像写入才算完成，因此整个 vdev 的写入延迟取决于 [.filename]#ada2p1#。在正常操作数量下出现高延迟，而 `zpool status` 中没有读取、写入或校验和错误，这通常表明磁盘正在内部重试，可能需要更换。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2001
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Scripts that must wait for background pool activity to finish can block on "
"`zpool wait`:"
msgstr "需要等待后台存储池活动完成的脚本可以通过 `zpool wait` 阻塞等待："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2005
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zpool wait -t scrub,resilver mypool\n"
msgstr "# zpool wait -t scrub,resilver mypool\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2009
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The command returns once none of the named activities, such as `scrub`, "
"`resilver`, `trim`, or `remove`, are in progress.  See man:zpool-wait[8] for "
"the full list of activities."
msgstr "当列出的活动（例如 `scrub`、`resilver`、`trim` 或 `remove`）全部结束后，该命令才会返回。完整的活动列表请参阅 man:zpool-wait[8]。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2014
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`zpool status`, `zpool list`, `zpool get`, and `zfs list` accept `-j` to "
"produce JSON output, which is more robust for scripts to parse than the "
"human-readable tables.  JSON output requires OpenZFS 2.3 or later, first "
"available in FreeBSD 15.0."
msgstr "`zpool status`、`zpool list`、`zpool get` 和 `zfs list` 支持 `-j`，可生成 JSON 输出；与便于人类阅读的表格相比，JSON 输出更适合脚本可靠地解析。JSON 输出需要 OpenZFS 2.3 或更高版本，该功能最早在 FreeBSD 15.0 中提供。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2017
#, no-wrap
msgid "Splitting a Storage Pool"
msgstr "分割存储池"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2024
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"ZFS can split a pool consisting of one or more mirror vdevs into two pools.  "
"Unless otherwise specified, ZFS detaches the last member of each mirror and "
"creates a new pool containing the same data.  Be sure to make a dry run of "
"the operation with `-n` first.  This displays the details of the requested "
"operation without actually performing it.  This helps confirm that the "
"operation will do what the user intends."
msgstr ""
"由一个或多个镜像 vdev 所组成的存储池可以切分开成两个存储池。除非有另外指定，"
"否则每个镜像的最后一个成员会被分离来然用来建立一个含有相同资料的新存储池。在"
"做这个操作的第一次应先使用 <option>-n</option>，会显示预计会做的操作而不会真"
"的执行，这可以协助确认操作是否与使用者所要的相同。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2026
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`zfs` Administration"
msgstr "`zfs` 管理"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2030
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `zfs` utility can create, destroy, and manage all existing ZFS datasets "
"within a pool.  To manage the pool itself, use crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool,"
"`zpool`]."
msgstr "`zfs` 工具可以在存储池中创建、销毁和管理所有现有的 ZFS 数据集。要管理存储池本身，请使用 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool,`zpool`]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2032
#, no-wrap
msgid "Creating and Destroying Datasets"
msgstr "创建和删除数据集"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2043
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Unlike traditional disks and volume managers, space in ZFS is _not_ "
"preallocated.  With traditional file systems, after partitioning and "
"assigning the space, there is no way to add a new file system without adding "
"a new disk.  With ZFS, creating new file systems is possible at any time.  "
"Each crossref:zfs[zfs-term-dataset,_dataset_] has properties including "
"features like compression, deduplication, caching, and quotas, as well as "
"other useful properties like readonly, case sensitivity, network file "
"sharing, and a mount point.  Nesting datasets within each other is possible "
"and child datasets will inherit properties from their ancestors.  crossref:"
"zfs[zfs-zfs-allow,Delegate], crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-send,replicate], crossref:"
"zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot,snapshot], crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-jail,jail] allows "
"administering and destroying each dataset as a unit.  Creating a separate "
"dataset for each different type or set of files has advantages.  The "
"drawbacks to having a large number of datasets are that some commands like "
"`zfs list` will be slower, and that mounting of hundreds or even thousands "
"of datasets will slow the FreeBSD boot process."
msgstr ""
"不同于传统的磁盘与磁盘区管理程序（Volume manager），在 <acronym>ZFS</"
"acronym> 中的空间并<emphasis>不</emphasis>会预先分配。传统的文件系统在分割与"
"分配空间完后，若没有增加新的磁盘便无法再增加额外的文件系统。在 <acronym>ZFS</"
"acronym>，可以随时建立新的文件系统，每个数据集（<link linkend=\"zfs-term-"
"dataset\"><emphasis>Dataset</emphasis></link>）都有自己的属性，包含压缩"
"（Compression）、去重复（Deduplication）、快取（Caching）与配额（Quota）功能"
"以及其他有用的属性如只读（Readonly）、区分大小写（Case sensitivity）、网路文"
"件分享（Network file sharing）以及挂载点（Mount point）。数据集可以存在于其他"
"数据集中，且子数据集会继承其父数据集的属性。每个数据集都可以作为一个单位来管"
"理、委托（<link linkend=\"zfs-zfs-allow\">Delegate</link>）、备份（<link "
"linkend=\"zfs-zfs-send\">Replicate</link>）、快照（<link linkend=\"zfs-zfs-"
"snapshot\">Snapshot</link>）、监禁（<link linkend=\"zfs-zfs-jail\">Jail</"
"link>） 与摧毁（Destroy），替每种不同类型或集合的文件建立各别的数据集还有许多"
"的好处。唯一的缺点是在当有非常大数量的数据集时，部份指令例如 <command>zfs "
"list</command> 会变的较缓慢，且挂载上百个或其至上千个数据集可能会使 FreeBSD "
"的开机程序变慢。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:2045
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Create a new dataset and enable crossref:zfs[zfs-term-compression-lz4,LZ4 "
