#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4203
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "ZFS Features and Terminology"
msgstr "ZFS 功能与术语"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4212
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"ZFS is fundamentally different from traditional file systems.  ZFS combines "
"the roles of file system and volume manager, enabling the addition of new "
"storage devices to a live system and making the new space available on the "
"existing file systems in that pool at once.  By combining the traditionally "
"separate roles, ZFS overcomes previous limitations that prevented RAID "
"groups from growing.  A _vdev_ is a top level device in a pool and can be a "
"simple disk or a RAID transformation such as a mirror or RAID-Z array.  ZFS "
"file systems (called _datasets_) each have access to the combined free space "
"of the entire pool.  Used blocks from the pool decrease the space available "
"to each file system.  This approach avoids the common pitfall with extensive "
"partitioning where free space becomes fragmented across the partitions."
msgstr ""
"<acronym>ZFS</acronym> 是一个从本质上与众不同的文件系统，由于它并非只是一个文"
"件系统，<acronym>ZFS</acronym> 结合了文件系统及磁盘区管理程序，让额外的储存设"
"备可以即时的加入到系统并可让既有的文件系统立即使用这些在存储池中空间。透过结"
"合传统区分为二的两个角色，<acronym>ZFS</acronym> 能够克服以往 <acronym>RAID</"
"acronym> 磁盘群组无法扩充的限制。每个在存储池顶层的设备称作<emphasis>vdev</"
"emphasis>，其可以是一个简单的磁盘或是一个<acronym>RAID</acronym> 如镜像或"
"<acronym>RAID-Z</acronym > 阵列。 <acronym>ZFS</acronym> 的文件系统（称作"
"<emphasis>数据集（Dataset）</emphasis>）每一个数据集均可存取整个存池所共通的"
"可用空间，随着使用存储池来配置空间区块，存储池能给每个文件系统使用的可用空间"
"就会减少，这个方法可以避免扩大分割区会使的可用空间分散分割区之间的常见问题。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4218
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-pool]]pool"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-pool]]存储池"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4221
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A storage _pool_ is the most basic building block of ZFS. A pool consists of one or more vdevs, the underlying devices that store the data. A pool is then used to create one or more file systems (datasets) or block devices (volumes).\n"
"These datasets and volumes share the pool of remaining free space. Each pool is uniquely identified by a name and a GUID. Pools created by modern OpenZFS are at pool version 5000; from that version on, individual capabilities are managed by _feature flags_ rather than the version number. See man:zpool-features[7] and crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-upgrade,Upgrading a Storage Pool] for details."
msgstr "存储 _pool_ 是 ZFS 最基本的构建块。存储池由一个或多个 vdev 组成，vdev 是用于存储数据的底层设备。随后可使用存储池创建一个或多个文件系统（数据集）或块设备（卷）。\n这些数据集和卷共享存储池中剩余的可用空间。每个存储池都由名称和 GUID 唯一标识。现代 OpenZFS 创建的存储池版本为 5000；从该版本开始，各项功能由 _功能标志_ 管理，而不再由版本号管理。详情请参阅 man:zpool-features[7] 和 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-upgrade,升级存储池]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4222
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-vdev]]vdev Types"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-vdev]]vdev 类型"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4256
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A pool consists of one or more vdevs, which themselves are a single disk or a group of disks, transformed to a RAID. When using a lot of vdevs, ZFS spreads data across the vdevs to increase performance and maximize usable space. All vdevs must be at least 64 MB in size.\n"
"\n"
"* [[zfs-term-vdev-disk]] _Disk_ - The most basic vdev type is a standard block device. This can be an entire disk (such as [.filename]#/dev/ada0#) or a partition ([.filename]#/dev/ada0p3#). On FreeBSD, there is no performance penalty for using a partition rather than the entire disk. This differs from recommendations made by the Solaris documentation.\n"
"+\n"
"[CAUTION]\n"
"====\n"
"Using an entire disk as part of a bootable pool is strongly discouraged, as this may render the pool unbootable.\n"
"Likewise, you should not use an entire disk as part of a mirror or RAID-Z vdev.\n"
"Reliably determining the size of an unpartitioned disk at boot time is impossible and there's no place to put in boot code.\n"
"====\n"
"\n"
"* [[zfs-term-vdev-file]] _File_ - Regular files may make up ZFS pools, which is useful for testing and experimentation. Use the full path to the file as the device path in `zpool create`.\n"
"* [[zfs-term-vdev-mirror]] _Mirror_ - When creating a mirror, specify the `mirror` keyword followed by the list of member devices for the mirror. A mirror consists of two or more devices, writing all data to all member devices. A mirror vdev will hold as much data as its smallest member. A mirror vdev can withstand the failure of all but one of its members without losing any data.\n"
"+\n"
"[NOTE]\n"
"====\n"
"To upgrade a regular single disk vdev to a mirror vdev at any time, use `zpool crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-attach,attach]`.\n"
"====\n"
"\n"
"* [[zfs-term-vdev-raidz]] _RAID-Z_ - ZFS uses RAID-Z, a variation on standard RAID-5 that offers better distribution of parity and eliminates the \"RAID-5 write hole\" in which the data and parity information become inconsistent after an unexpected restart. ZFS supports three levels of RAID-Z which provide varying levels of redundancy in exchange for decreasing levels of usable storage. ZFS uses RAID-Z1 through RAID-Z3 based on the number of parity devices in the array and the number of disks which can fail before the pool stops being operational.\n"
"+\n"
"In a RAID-Z1 configuration with four disks, each 1 TB, usable storage is 3 TB and the pool will still be able to operate in degraded mode with one faulted disk. If another disk goes offline before replacing and resilvering the faulted disk would result in losing all pool data.\n"
"+\n"
"In a RAID-Z3 configuration with eight disks of 1 TB, the volume will provide 5 TB of usable space and still be able to operate with three faulted disks. The traditional recommendation is no more than nine disks in a single vdev. If more disks make up the configuration, the recommendation is to divide them into separate vdevs and stripe the pool data across them.\n"
"+\n"
"A configuration of two RAID-Z2 vdevs consisting of 8 disks each would create something like a RAID-60 array. A RAID-Z group's storage capacity is about the size of the smallest disk multiplied by the number of non-parity disks. Four 1 TB disks in RAID-Z1 has an effective size of about 3 TB, and an array of eight 1 TB disks in RAID-Z3 will yield 5 TB of usable space.\n"
"+\n"
"Growing a raidz vdev one disk at a time is possible with crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-raidz-expansion,RAID-Z expansion], which requires OpenZFS 2.3 or later, first available in FreeBSD 15.0.\n"
"* [[zfs-term-vdev-draid]] _dRAID_ - A variant of RAID-Z that distributes data, parity, and spare capacity across all member disks using fixed-width stripes. Instead of dedicated hot spare disks, dRAID provides _distributed spares_: spare capacity spread over every member disk, allowing a failed disk to rebuild sequentially onto all remaining disks at once and restoring redundancy much faster than a traditional resilver onto a single spare. Specify a dRAID vdev as `draid[parity][:datad][:childrenc][:sparess]`, as described in man:zpoolconcepts[7]. See crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-draid,dRAID Pools] for details.\n"
"* [[zfs-term-vdev-spare]] _Spare_ - ZFS has a special pseudo-vdev type for keeping track of available hot spares. When man:zfsd[8] is enabled, ZFS deploys installed hot spares automatically to replace failed devices; otherwise, configure them manually to replace the failed device using `zpool replace`. See crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-spares,Hot Spares and Automatic Replacement with zfsd] for details.\n"
"* [[zfs-term-vdev-log]] _Log_ - Every pool has a ZFS Intent Log (crossref:zfs[zfs-term-zil,ZIL]), stored on the regular pool devices by default. A dedicated log vdev, often called a SLOG, moves the intent log to a separate device, typically an SSD. Having a dedicated log device improves the performance of applications with a high volume of synchronous writes like databases. Mirroring of log devices is possible, but RAID-Z is not supported. If using a lot of log devices, writes will be load-balanced across them. See crossref:zfs[zfs-advanced-zil-slog,\"Synchronous Writes, the ZIL, and SLOG\"] for details.\n"
"* [[zfs-term-vdev-cache]] _Cache_ - Adding a cache vdev to a pool will add the storage of the cache to the crossref:zfs[zfs-term-l2arc,L2ARC]. Mirroring cache devices is impossible. Since a cache device stores only new copies of existing data, there is no risk of data loss.\n"
"* [[zfs-term-vdev-special]] _Special/Dedup_ - Allocation class vdevs that store pool metadata, optionally small file blocks (controlled by the `special_small_blocks` dataset property), and deduplication tables on fast devices such as SSDs, speeding up a pool of slower disks. These vdevs are pool-critical: losing a special or dedup vdev loses the pool, so give them the same level of redundancy as the data vdevs. See crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-special,Special Allocation Classes] for details."
msgstr "存储池由一个或多个 vdev 组成，每个 vdev 本身可以是单个磁盘，也可以是一组经过 RAID 转换的磁盘。使用多个 vdev 时，ZFS 会将数据分布到各个 vdev 上，以提高性能并最大限度地利用可用空间。所有 vdev 的大小都必须至少为 64 MB。\n\n* [[zfs-term-vdev-disk]] __磁盘__ - 最基本的 vdev 类型是标准块设备。它可以是整块磁盘（例如 [.filename]#/dev/ada0#）或分区（[.filename]#/dev/ada0p3#）。在 FreeBSD 上，使用分区而非整块磁盘不会造成性能损失。这与 Solaris 文档中的建议不同。\n+\n[CAUTION]\n====\n强烈建议不要将整块磁盘用于可启动存储池，否则可能导致存储池无法启动。\n同样，也不应将整块磁盘用于镜像或 RAID-Z vdev。\n启动时无法可靠地确定未分区磁盘的大小，而且也没有地方存放引导代码。\n====\n\n* [[zfs-term-vdev-file]] __文件__ - 普通文件也可构成 ZFS 存储池，这对于测试和实验很有用。在 `zpool create` 中将文件的完整路径用作设备路径。\n* [[zfs-term-vdev-mirror]] __镜像__ - 创建镜像时，指定关键字 `mirror`，然后列出镜像的成员设备。镜像由两个或更多设备组成，并将所有数据写入所有成员设备。镜像 vdev 可存储的数据量取决于其最小成员设备。除一个成员设备外，镜像 vdev 可以承受其他所有成员设备发生故障而不丢失数据。\n+\n[NOTE]\n====\n要随时将普通的单磁盘 vdev 升级为镜像 vdev，请使用 `zpool crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-attach,attach]`。\n====\n\n* [[zfs-term-vdev-raidz]] __RAID-Z__ - ZFS 使用 RAID-Z，这是标准 RAID-5 的一种变体，具有更好的校验数据分布，并消除了「RAID-5 写入漏洞」——意外重启后，数据与校验信息可能变得不一致。ZFS 支持三个级别的 RAID-Z，在提供不同冗余级别的同时，可用存储容量也依次降低。ZFS 根据阵列中的校验设备数量以及存储池停止运行前可发生故障的磁盘数量，使用 RAID-Z1 至 RAID-Z3。\n+\n在由四块 1 TB 磁盘组成的 RAID-Z1 配置中，可用存储空间为 3 TB；即使一块磁盘发生故障，存储池仍可在降级模式下运行。如果在更换故障磁盘并完成重新同步之前，另一块磁盘也离线，所有存储池数据都将丢失。\n+\n在由八块 1 TB 磁盘组成的 RAID-Z3 配置中，卷可提供 5 TB 可用空间，并且即使三块磁盘发生故障，仍可继续运行。传统建议是单个 vdev 中最多使用九块磁盘。如果配置包含更多磁盘，建议将其划分为多个独立 vdev，并在这些 vdev 之间条带化存储池数据。\n+\n由两个 RAID-Z2 vdev 组成的配置，每个 vdev 含 8 块磁盘，效果类似 RAID-60 阵列。RAID-Z 组的存储容量约等于最小磁盘的容量乘以非校验磁盘的数量。四块 1 TB 磁盘组成的 RAID-Z1 有效容量约为 3 TB，而八块 1 TB 磁盘组成的 RAID-Z3 阵列可提供 5 TB 可用空间。\n+\n使用 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-raidz-expansion,RAID-Z 扩展]可以逐次向 raidz vdev 添加一块磁盘；此功能需要 OpenZFS 2.3 或更高版本，首次在 FreeBSD 15.0 中提供。\n* [[zfs-term-vdev-draid]] __dRAID__ - RAID-Z 的一种变体，使用固定宽度条带将数据、校验信息和备用容量分布到所有成员磁盘上。dRAID 不使用专用热备磁盘，而是提供 __分布式备用容量__：将备用容量分散到每块成员磁盘上，使故障磁盘能够同时顺序重建到所有剩余磁盘，从而比传统方式将数据重新同步到单块备用磁盘更快地恢复冗余。按照 man:zpoolconcepts[7] 中的说明，将 dRAID vdev 指定为 `draid[parity][:datad][:childrenc][:sparess]`。详情请参阅 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-draid,dRAID 存储池]。\n* [[zfs-term-vdev-spare]] __备用设备__ - ZFS 有一种特殊的伪 vdev 类型，用于跟踪可用的热备设备。启用 man:zfsd[8] 后，ZFS 会自动部署已安装的热备设备来替换故障设备；否则，应使用 `zpool replace` 手动配置替换。详情请参阅 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-spares,热备设备与 zfsd 自动替换]。\n* [[zfs-term-vdev-log]] __日志__ - 每个存储池都有一个 ZFS 意图日志（crossref:zfs[zfs-term-zil,ZIL]），默认存储在普通存储池设备上。专用日志 vdev 通常称为 SLOG，会将意图日志移至单独的设备，通常是 SSD。专用日志设备可以提高同步写入量较大的应用程序（如数据库）的性能。日志设备可以镜像，但不支持 RAID-Z。使用多个日志设备时，写入会在这些设备之间进行负载均衡。详情请参阅 crossref:zfs[zfs-advanced-zil-slog,\"同步写入、ZIL 与 SLOG\"]。\n* [[zfs-term-vdev-cache]] __缓存__ - 向存储池添加缓存 vdev 会将其存储空间加入 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-l2arc,L2ARC]。缓存设备无法镜像。由于缓存设备只存储现有数据的新副本，因此不会有数据丢失风险。\n* [[zfs-term-vdev-special]] __特殊/去重__ - 分配类 vdev，用于在 SSD 等快速设备上存储存储池元数据、可选的小文件块（由数据集属性 `special_small_blocks` 控制）以及去重表，从而加快较慢磁盘组成的存储池。这些 vdev 对存储池至关重要：特殊或去重 vdev 丢失会导致整个存储池丢失，因此应为它们配置与数据 vdev 相同级别的冗余。详情请参阅 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-special,特殊分配类]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4257
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-txg]] Transaction Group (TXG)"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-txg]]事务组（TXG）"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4278
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Transaction Groups are the way ZFS groups blocks changes together and writes them to the pool. Transaction groups are the atomic unit that ZFS uses to ensure consistency. ZFS assigns each transaction group a unique 64-bit consecutive identifier. There can be up to three active transaction groups at a time, one in each of these three states:\n"
"\n"
"* _Open_ - A new transaction group begins in the open state and accepts new\n"
"  writes. There is always a transaction group in the open state, but the\n"
"  transaction group may refuse new writes if it has reached a limit. Once the\n"
"  open transaction group has reached a limit, or reaching the\n"
"  crossref:zfs[zfs-advanced-tuning,`vfs.zfs.txg.timeout`], the transaction group advances to the next state.\n"
"* _Quiescing_ - A short state that allows any pending operations to finish without blocking the creation of a new open transaction group. Once all the transactions in the group have completed, the transaction group advances to the final state.\n"
"* _Syncing_ - Write all the data in the transaction group to stable storage.\n"
"  This process will in turn change other data, such as metadata and space maps,\n"
"  that ZFS will also write to stable storage. The process of syncing involves\n"
"  several passes. On the first and biggest, all the changed data blocks; next\n"
"  come the metadata, which may take several passes to complete. Since allocating\n"
"  space for the data blocks generates new metadata, the syncing state cannot\n"
"  finish until a pass completes that does not use any new space. The syncing\n"
"  state is also where _synctasks_ complete. Synctasks are administrative\n"
"  operations such as creating or destroying snapshots and datasets that complete\n"
"  the uberblock change. Once the sync state completes the transaction group in\n"
"  the quiescing state advances to the syncing state. All administrative\n"
"  functions, such as crossref:zfs[zfs-term-snapshot,`snapshot`] write as part of the transaction group. ZFS adds a created synctask to the open transaction group, and that group advances as fast as possible to the syncing state to reduce the latency of administrative commands."
msgstr "事务组是 ZFS 将块更改分组并写入存储池的方式。事务组是 ZFS 用于确保一致性的原子单位。ZFS 为每个事务组分配一个唯一且连续递增的 64 位标识符。任何时刻最多可有三个活动事务组，分别处于以下三种状态之一：\n\n* __打开__ - 新事务组以打开状态开始，并接受新的写入。始终有一个事务组处于打开状态，但如果达到限制，它可能会拒绝新的写入。当打开的事务组达到限制，或达到 crossref:zfs[zfs-advanced-tuning,`vfs.zfs.txg.timeout`] 所设定的时间时，该事务组会进入下一状态。\n* __静止__ - 一个短暂状态，允许所有待处理操作完成，同时不阻止创建新的打开事务组。组中的所有事务完成后，该事务组会进入最后一个状态。\n* __同步__ - 将事务组中的所有数据写入稳定存储。此过程还会更改其他数据，例如元数据和空间映射，ZFS 也会将这些数据写入稳定存储。同步过程分多个阶段进行。第一阶段写入所有已更改的数据块，工作量最大；随后写入元数据，可能需要多个阶段才能完成。由于为数据块分配空间会生成新的元数据，因此只有某个阶段不再使用新空间时，同步状态才能结束。同步状态也是 __同步任务__ 完成的阶段。同步任务是管理操作，例如创建或销毁快照和数据集；这些操作通过更改 uberblock 完成。同步状态完成后，处于静止状态的事务组会进入同步状态。所有管理操作（例如 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-snapshot,`snapshot`]）都会作为事务组的一部分写入。ZFS 会将新创建的同步任务加入打开的事务组，并尽快推动该组进入同步状态，以降低管理命令的延迟。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4279
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-arc]]Adaptive Replacement Cache (ARC)"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-arc]]自适应替换缓存（ARC）"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4281
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "ZFS uses an Adaptive Replacement Cache (ARC), rather than a more traditional Least Recently Used (LRU) cache. An LRU cache is a simple list of items in the cache, sorted by how recently object was used, adding new items to the head of the list. When the cache is full, evicting items from the tail of the list makes room for more active objects. An ARC consists of four lists; the Most Recently Used (MRU) and Most Frequently Used (MFU) objects, plus a ghost list for each. These ghost lists track evicted objects to prevent adding them back to the cache. This increases the cache hit ratio by avoiding objects that have a history of occasional use. Another advantage of using both an MRU and MFU is that scanning an entire file system would evict all data from an MRU or LRU cache in favor of this freshly accessed content. With ZFS, there is also an MFU that tracks the most frequently used objects, and the cache of the most commonly accessed blocks remains."
msgstr "ZFS 使用自适应替换缓存（ARC），而不是更传统的最近最少使用（LRU）缓存。LRU 缓存是一个简单的项目列表，按对象最近使用的时间排序，新项目添加到列表头部。缓存已满时，从列表尾部逐出项目，为更活跃的对象腾出空间。ARC 由四个列表组成：最近使用（MRU）和最常使用（MFU）对象列表，以及各自对应的幽灵列表。这些幽灵列表会跟踪已逐出的对象，防止它们重新加入缓存。这样可以避免缓存偶尔使用过的对象，从而提高缓存命中率。同时使用 MRU 和 MFU 的另一个优点是，扫描整个文件系统时，传统缓存会用刚访问的内容替换 MRU 或 LRU 缓存中的所有数据。ZFS 还使用 MFU 跟踪最常使用的对象，因此最常访问的数据块仍保留在缓存中。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4282
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-l2arc]]L2ARC"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-l2arc]]L2ARC"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4298
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"L2ARC is the second level of the ZFS caching system. RAM stores the primary\n"
"ARC. Since the amount of available RAM is often limited, ZFS can also use\n"
"crossref:zfs[zfs-term-vdev-cache,cache vdevs]. Solid State Disks (SSDs) are\n"
"often used as these cache devices due to their higher speed and lower latency\n"
"compared to traditional spinning disks. L2ARC is entirely optional, but having\n"
"one will increase read speeds for cached files on the SSD instead of having to\n"
"read from the regular disks. L2ARC can also speed up\n"
"crossref:zfs[zfs-term-deduplication,deduplication] because a deduplication table\n"
"(DDT) that does not fit in RAM but does fit in the L2ARC will be much faster\n"
"than a DDT that must read from disk.\n"
"Since OpenZFS 2.0, the L2ARC is persistent: after a reboot, ZFS rebuilds the cache contents from the headers stored on the cache device instead of starting with an empty cache.\n"
"Limits on the data rate added to the cache devices prevent prematurely wearing out SSDs with extra writes.\n"
"Until the cache is full (the first block evicted to make room), writes to the L2ARC limit to the sum of the write limit and the boost limit, and afterwards limit to the write limit.\n"
"A pair of man:sysctl[8] values control these rate limits: `vfs.zfs.l2arc.write_max` controls the number of bytes written to the cache per second, while `vfs.zfs.l2arc.write_boost` adds to this limit until the first eviction from the cache.\n"
"See crossref:zfs[zfs-advanced-tuning,Tuning] for details."
msgstr "L2ARC 是 ZFS 缓存系统的第二级。主 ARC 存储在 RAM 中。由于可用 RAM 通常有限，ZFS 也可以使用 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-vdev-cache,缓存 vdev]。与传统旋转磁盘相比，固态硬盘（SSD）速度更快、延迟更低，因此常用作这些缓存设备。L2ARC 完全可选，但启用后，缓存文件的读取速度会更快，因为可以从 SSD 读取，而不必从普通磁盘读取。L2ARC 还可以加快 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-deduplication,去重]：如果去重表（DDT）无法放入 RAM，但可以放入 L2ARC，其访问速度会远快于必须从磁盘读取的 DDT。\n从 OpenZFS 2.0 开始，L2ARC 具有持久性：重启后，ZFS 会根据缓存设备上存储的标头重建缓存内容，而不是从空缓存开始。\n对写入缓存设备的数据速率进行限制，可以避免过多写入导致 SSD 过早磨损。\n在缓存填满之前（即首次逐出数据块以腾出空间之前），写入 L2ARC 的速率上限为写入限制与提升限制之和；之后则仅受写入限制约束。\n两个 man:sysctl[8] 值用于控制这些速率限制：`vfs.zfs.l2arc.write_max` 控制每秒写入缓存的字节数，而 `vfs.zfs.l2arc.write_boost` 会在首次从缓存逐出数据之前提高此限制。\n详情请参阅 crossref:zfs[zfs-advanced-tuning,调整]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4299
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-zil]]ZIL"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-zil]]ZIL"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4301
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "The ZFS Intent Log (ZIL) is the on-disk record that ZFS uses to replay synchronous writes after a crash. Every pool has a ZIL; by default it occupies a small amount of space on the regular pool devices. When an application requests a synchronous write (a guarantee that the data is stored to disk rather than merely cached for later writes), ZFS commits the data to the ZIL first and flushes it out to the regular storage with the next transaction group. Moving the ZIL to a dedicated crossref:zfs[zfs-term-vdev-log,log vdev] (SLOG) on a device faster than the main storage, such as an SSD, greatly reduces latency and improves performance. Synchronous workloads like databases will profit from a fast ZIL alone. Regular asynchronous writes such as copying files will not use the ZIL at all. See crossref:zfs[zfs-advanced-zil-slog,\"Synchronous Writes, the ZIL, and SLOG\"] for details."
msgstr "ZFS 意图日志（ZIL）是 ZFS 用于在崩溃后重放同步写入的磁盘记录。每个存储池都有 ZIL；默认情况下，它会占用普通存储池设备上的少量空间。当应用程序请求同步写入（保证数据已存储到磁盘，而不仅仅是缓存起来等待稍后写入）时，ZFS 会先将数据提交到 ZIL，然后在下一个事务组中将其刷新到常规存储设备。将 ZIL 移至速度快于主存储设备（例如 SSD）的专用 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-vdev-log,日志 vdev]（SLOG），可以显著降低延迟并提高性能。数据库等同步工作负载仅使用快速 ZIL 就能受益。复制文件等常规异步写入完全不会使用 ZIL。详情请参阅 crossref:zfs[zfs-advanced-zil-slog,\"同步写入、ZIL 与 SLOG\"]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4302
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-cow]]Copy-On-Write"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-cow]]写时复制"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4304
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Unlike a traditional file system, ZFS writes a different block rather than overwriting the old data in place. When completing this write the metadata updates to point to the new location. When a shorn write (a system crash or power loss in the middle of writing a file) occurs, the entire original contents of the file are still available and ZFS discards the incomplete write. This also means that ZFS does not require a man:fsck[8] after an unexpected shutdown."
msgstr "与传统文件系统不同，ZFS 会将数据写入不同的数据块，而不是就地覆盖旧数据。写入完成后，元数据会更新为指向新位置。如果发生写入撕裂（在写入文件过程中系统崩溃或断电），文件的全部原始内容仍然可用，ZFS 会丢弃未完成的写入。这也意味着意外关机后 ZFS 不需要运行 man:fsck[8]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4305
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-dataset]]Dataset"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-dataset]]数据集"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4315
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"_Dataset_ is the generic term for a ZFS file system, volume, snapshot or clone.\n"
"Each dataset has a unique name in the format _poolname/path@snapshot_. The root\n"
"of the pool is a dataset as well. Child datasets have hierarchical names like\n"
"directories. For example, _mypool/home_, the home dataset, is a child of\n"
"_mypool_ and inherits properties from it. Expand this further by creating\n"
"_mypool/home/user_. This grandchild dataset will inherit properties from the\n"
"parent and grandparent. Set properties on a child to override the defaults\n"
"inherited from the parent and grandparent. Administration of datasets and their\n"
"children can be crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-allow,delegated]."
msgstr "__数据集__ 是 ZFS 文件系统、卷、快照或克隆的统称。\n每个数据集都有唯一名称，格式为 _poolname/path@snapshot_。存储池的根本身也是一个数据集。子数据集具有类似目录的层级名称。例如，_mypool/home_（主目录数据集）是 _mypool_ 的子数据集，并会继承其属性。还可以继续创建 _mypool/home/user_。这个孙级数据集会继承父级和祖父级的属性。在子数据集上设置属性可覆盖从父级和祖父级继承的默认值。数据集及其子数据集的管理可以通过 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-allow,委托]完成。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4316
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-filesystem]]File system"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-filesystem]]文件系统"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4318
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "A ZFS dataset is most often used as a file system. Like most other file systems, a ZFS file system mounts somewhere in the systems directory hierarchy and contains files and directories of its own with permissions, flags, and other metadata."
msgstr "ZFS 数据集最常见的用途是作为文件系统。与大多数其他文件系统一样，ZFS 文件系统会挂载到系统目录层次结构中的某个位置，并包含自身的文件和目录，以及权限、标志和其他元数据。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4319
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-volume]]Volume"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-volume]]卷"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4321
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "ZFS can also create volumes, which appear as disk devices. Volumes have a lot of the same features as datasets, including copy-on-write, snapshots, clones, and checksumming. Volumes can be useful for running other file system formats on top of ZFS, such as UFS virtualization, or exporting iSCSI extents."
msgstr "ZFS 还可以创建表现为磁盘设备的卷。卷具有许多与数据集相同的功能，包括写时复制、快照、克隆和校验。卷可用于在 ZFS 之上运行其他文件系统格式，例如虚拟化 UFS，或导出 iSCSI 扩展。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4322
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-snapshot]]Snapshot"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-snapshot]]快照"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4342
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The crossref:zfs[zfs-term-cow,copy-on-write] (COW) design of ZFS allows for\n"
"nearly instantaneous, consistent snapshots with arbitrary names. After taking a\n"
"snapshot of a dataset, or a recursive snapshot of a parent dataset that will\n"
"include all child datasets, new data goes to new blocks, but without reclaiming\n"
"the old blocks as free space. The snapshot contains the original file system\n"
"version and the live file system contains any changes made since taking the\n"
"snapshot using no other space. New data written to the live file system uses new\n"
"blocks to store this data. The snapshot will grow as the blocks are no longer\n"
"used in the live file system, but in the snapshot alone. Mounting these snapshots\n"
"read-only allows recovering previous file versions. A\n"
"crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot-rollback,rollback] of a live file system to a specific\n"
"snapshot is possible, undoing any changes that took place after taking the\n"
"snapshot. Each block in the pool has a reference counter which keeps track of\n"
"the snapshots, clones, datasets, or volumes use that block. As files and\n"
"snapshots get deleted, the reference count decreases, reclaiming the free space\n"
"when no longer referencing a block. Marking snapshots with a\n"
"crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot-hold,hold] means any attempt to destroy it\n"
"returns an `EBUSY` error. Each snapshot can have holds with a unique name each.\n"
"The crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot-hold,release] command removes the hold so the snapshot can be deleted. Snapshots, cloning, and rolling back works on volumes, but independently mounting does not."
msgstr "ZFS 的 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-cow,写时复制]（COW）设计支持近乎即时地创建名称任意且一致的快照。对数据集创建快照，或对父数据集创建递归快照（其中包含所有子数据集）后，新数据会写入新的数据块，但旧数据块不会被回收为空闲空间。快照保留原始文件系统版本，而活动文件系统包含创建快照以来所做的所有更改，且不额外占用空间。写入活动文件系统的新数据会使用新的数据块。随着数据块不再被活动文件系统使用、而仅被快照引用，快照会增大。以只读方式挂载这些快照即可恢复以前版本的文件。可以将活动文件系统 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot-rollback,回滚]到特定快照，撤销创建快照后发生的所有更改。存储池中的每个数据块都有一个引用计数器，用于跟踪哪些快照、克隆、数据集或卷使用该数据块。删除文件和快照时，引用计数会减少；当不再有引用时，空间就会被回收。为快照添加 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot-hold,保留标记]后，任何销毁该快照的尝试都会返回 `EBUSY` 错误。每个快照可以有多个名称各不相同的保留标记。crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot-hold,release] 命令会移除保留标记，使快照可以被删除。快照、克隆和回滚也适用于卷，但卷无法单独挂载。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4343
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-clone]]Clone"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-clone]]克隆"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4345
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Cloning a snapshot is also possible. A clone is a writable version of a snapshot, allowing the file system to fork as a new dataset. As with a snapshot, a clone initially consumes no new space. As new data written to a clone uses new blocks, the size of the clone grows. When blocks are overwritten in the cloned file system or volume, the reference count on the previous block decreases. Removing the snapshot upon which a clone bases is impossible because the clone depends on it. The snapshot is the parent, and the clone is the child. Clones can be _promoted_, reversing this dependency and making the clone the parent and the previous parent the child. This operation requires no new space. Since the amount of space used by the parent and child reverses, it may affect existing quotas and reservations."
msgstr "也可以克隆快照。克隆是快照的可写版本，可将文件系统分支为新的数据集。与快照一样，克隆初始不会占用额外空间。向克隆写入新数据时会使用新的数据块，因此克隆会增大。克隆文件系统或卷中的数据块被覆盖时，先前数据块的引用计数会减少。由于克隆依赖其基础快照，因此无法删除该快照。快照是父级，克隆是子级。克隆可以进行 __提升__，反转这种依赖关系，使克隆成为父级，而原父级成为子级。此操作不需要额外空间。由于父级和子级所用空间的归属会发生反转，现有配额和预留空间可能受到影响。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4346
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-bookmark]]Bookmark"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-bookmark]]书签"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4351
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A bookmark records the point in time at which a snapshot was taken, without keeping any of the snapshot data.\n"
"Bookmarks serve as the source of incremental crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-send,`zfs send`] streams, making it possible to destroy the snapshot on the sending side while retaining the ability to send further increments.\n"
"Create a bookmark from an existing snapshot with `zfs bookmark`.\n"
"See crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-bookmark,Bookmarks] for details."
msgstr "书签会记录创建快照的时间点，但不会保留任何快照数据。\n书签可作为增量 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-send,`zfs send`] 流的来源，从而可以在发送端销毁快照，同时保留继续发送后续增量的能力。\n使用 `zfs bookmark` 从现有快照创建书签。\n详情请参阅 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-bookmark,书签]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4352
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-hold]]Hold"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-hold]]保留标记"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4357
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A hold is a named tag placed on a snapshot that prevents its destruction.\n"
"Attempts to destroy a held snapshot fail with an `EBUSY` error until releasing every hold with `zfs release`.\n"
"Holds protect snapshots that backup and replication tools still depend on.\n"
"See crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot-hold,Snapshot Holds] for details."
msgstr "保留标记是添加到快照上的命名标签，可防止快照被销毁。\n在使用 `zfs release` 释放所有保留标记之前，销毁带有保留标记的快照会失败并返回 `EBUSY` 错误。\n保留标记可以保护备份和复制工具仍在依赖的快照。\n详情请参阅 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-snapshot-hold,快照保留标记]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4358
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-checksum]]Checksum"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-checksum]]校验和"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4377
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Every block is also checksummed. The checksum algorithm used is a per-dataset\n"
"property, see crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-set,`set`]. The checksum of each block is\n"
"transparently validated when read, allowing ZFS to detect silent corruption. If\n"
"the data read does not match the expected checksum, ZFS will attempt to recover\n"
"the data from any available redundancy, like mirrors or RAID-Z. Trigger a\n"
"validation of all checksums with crossref:zfs[zfs-term-scrub,`scrub`]. Checksum algorithms include:\n"
"\n"
"* `fletcher2`\n"
"* `fletcher4`\n"
"* `sha256`\n"
"* `sha512`\n"
"* `skein`\n"
"* `edonr`\n"
"* `blake3` (since FreeBSD 14.0)\n"
"\n"
"The `fletcher` algorithms are faster, but the cryptographic hashes (`sha256`, `sha512`, `skein`, `edonr`, and `blake3`) have a much lower chance of collisions at the cost of some performance.\n"
"The default value of `on` currently selects `fletcher4`; crossref:zfs[zfs-term-deduplication,deduplication] requires a cryptographic hash such as `sha256`.\n"
"Deactivating checksums is possible, but strongly discouraged."
msgstr "每个数据块也都有校验和。所用的校验和算法是每个数据集的属性，参见 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-set,`set`]。读取时会透明地验证每个数据块的校验和，使 ZFS 能够检测静默损坏。如果读取的数据与预期校验和不匹配，ZFS 会尝试使用任何可用的冗余（例如镜像或 RAID-Z）恢复数据。使用 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-scrub,`scrub`] 可触发对所有校验和的验证。校验和算法包括：\n\n* `fletcher2`\n* `fletcher4`\n* `sha256`\n* `sha512`\n* `skein`\n* `edonr`\n* `blake3`（自 FreeBSD 14.0 起）\n\n`fletcher` 算法速度更快，但加密哈希（`sha256`、`sha512`、`skein`、`edonr` 和 `blake3`）的碰撞概率要低得多，代价是一定的性能损失。\n目前，默认值 `on` 会选择 `fletcher4`；crossref:zfs[zfs-term-deduplication,去重] 需要使用 `sha256` 等加密哈希。\n虽然可以停用校验和，但强烈不建议这样做。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4378
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-compression]]Compression"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-compression]]压缩"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4395
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Each dataset has a compression property. Since OpenZFS 2.2, new datasets have compression enabled by default (`compression=on`, which selects LZ4). This causes compression of all new data written to the dataset. Beyond a reduction in space used, read and write throughput often increases because fewer blocks need reading or writing.\n"
"\n"
"[[zfs-term-compression-lz4]]\n"
"* _LZ4_ - Added in ZFS pool version 5000 (feature flags), LZ4 is the algorithm that `compression=on` selects and the recommended general-purpose choice. LZ4 works about 50% faster than LZJB when operating on compressible data, and is over three times faster when operating on uncompressible data. LZ4 also decompresses about 80% faster than LZJB. On modern CPUs, LZ4 can often compress at over 500 MB/s, and decompress at over 1.5 GB/s (per single CPU core).\n"
"\n"
"[[zfs-term-compression-zstd]]\n"
"* _ZSTD_ - Zstandard offers higher compression ratios than LZ4 with a configurable trade-off between speed and compression, ranging from the fast `zstd-fast` variants to `zstd-19` for maximum space savings. See crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-compression-zstd,Zstandard Compression] for details.\n"
"\n"
"[[zfs-term-compression-lzjb]]\n"
"* _LZJB_ - A legacy compression algorithm, created by Jeff Bonwick (one of the original creators of ZFS). LZJB offers good compression with less CPU overhead compared to GZIP. LZ4 has replaced it as the default algorithm; prefer LZ4 or ZSTD for new datasets.\n"
"\n"
"[[zfs-term-compression-gzip]]\n"
"* _GZIP_ - A popular stream compression algorithm available in ZFS. One of the main advantages of using GZIP is its configurable level of compression. When setting the `compress` property, the administrator can choose the level of compression, ranging from `gzip1`, the lowest level of compression, to `gzip9`, the highest level of compression. This gives the administrator control over how much CPU time to trade for saved disk space.\n"
"\n"
"[[zfs-term-compression-zle]]\n"
"* _ZLE_ - Zero Length Encoding is a special compression algorithm that compresses continuous runs of zeros alone. This compression algorithm is useful when the dataset contains large blocks of zeros."
msgstr "每个数据集都有一个压缩属性。自 OpenZFS 2.2 起，新数据集默认启用压缩（`compression=on`，它会选择 LZ4）。这会压缩写入数据集的所有新数据。除了减少空间占用外，由于需要读取或写入的块更少，读写吞吐量通常也会提高。\n\n[[zfs-term-compression-lz4]]\n* _LZ4_ - LZ4 在 ZFS 池版本 5000（功能标志）中引入，是 `compression=on` 选择的算法，也是推荐的通用选项。处理可压缩数据时，LZ4 的速度比 LZJB 快约 50%；处理不可压缩数据时，速度则快 3 倍以上。LZ4 的解压速度也比 LZJB 快约 80%。在现代 CPU 上，LZ4 的压缩速度通常可超过 500 MB/s，解压速度可超过 1.5 GB/s（以单个 CPU 核心计）。\n\n[[zfs-term-compression-zstd]]\n* _ZSTD_ - Zstandard 的压缩率高于 LZ4，并可在速度与压缩率之间进行可配置的权衡，范围从快速的 `zstd-fast` 变体到最大限度节省空间的 `zstd-19`。详情请参见 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-compression-zstd,Zstandard 压缩]。\n\n[[zfs-term-compression-lzjb]]\n* _LZJB_ - 一种旧式压缩算法，由 Jeff Bonwick（ZFS 的最初创建者之一）创作。与 GZIP 相比，LZJB 的压缩效果良好且 CPU 开销较低。LZ4 已取代它成为默认算法；新数据集建议使用 LZ4 或 ZSTD。\n\n[[zfs-term-compression-gzip]]\n* _GZIP_ - ZFS 中提供的一种流压缩算法，广受欢迎。使用 GZIP 的主要优势之一是其压缩级别可配置。设置 `compress` 属性时，管理员可以选择压缩级别，从最低级别的 `gzip1` 到最高级别的 `gzip9`。这让管理员可以控制以多少 CPU 时间换取磁盘空间节省。\n\n[[zfs-term-compression-zle]]\n* _ZLE_ - 零长度编码是一种特殊的压缩算法，只压缩连续出现的零。数据集包含大量零块时，这种压缩算法很有用。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4396
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-copies]]Copies"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-copies]]副本"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4400
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When set to a value greater than 1, the `copies` property instructs ZFS to\n"
"maintain copies of each block in the crossref:zfs[zfs-term-filesystem,file\n"
"system] or crossref:zfs[zfs-term-volume,volume]. Setting this property on important datasets provides added redundancy from which to recover a block that does not match its checksum. In pools without redundancy, the copies feature is the single form of redundancy. The copies feature can recover from a single bad sector or other forms of minor corruption, but it does not protect the pool from the loss of an entire disk."
msgstr "将 `copies` 属性设置为大于 1 的值时，ZFS 会在 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-filesystem,文件系统]或 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-volume,卷]中保留每个块的多个副本。在重要数据集上设置此属性，可增加冗余，以便从校验和不匹配的块中恢复。在没有冗余的池中，`copies` 功能是唯一的冗余形式。它可以从单个坏扇区或其他轻微损坏中恢复，但无法保护池免受整块磁盘丢失的影响。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4401
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-deduplication]]Deduplication"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-deduplication]]重复数据删除"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4405
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Checksums make it possible to detect duplicate blocks when writing data. With deduplication, the reference count of an existing, identical block increases, saving storage space. ZFS keeps a deduplication table (DDT) in memory to detect duplicate blocks. The table contains a list of unique checksums, the location of those blocks, and a reference count. When writing new data, ZFS calculates checksums and compares them to the list. When finding a match it uses the existing block. Using the SHA256 checksum algorithm with deduplication provides a secure cryptographic hash. Deduplication is tunable. If `dedup` is `on`, then a matching checksum means that the data is identical. Setting `dedup` to `verify`, ZFS performs a byte-for-byte check on the data ensuring they are actually identical. If the data is not identical, ZFS will note the hash collision and store the two blocks separately. As the DDT must store the hash of each unique block, it consumes a large amount of memory. A general rule of thumb is 5-6 GB of RAM per 1 TB of deduplicated data. In situations not practical to have enough RAM to keep the entire DDT in memory, performance will suffer greatly as the DDT must read from disk before writing each new block. Deduplication can use L2ARC to store the DDT, providing a middle ground between fast system memory and slower disks. Consider using compression instead, which often provides nearly as much space savings without the increased memory.\n"
"_Fast dedup_ batches DDT updates in a log, allows pruning stale entries with `zpool ddtprune`, and caps the table size with the `dedup_table_quota` pool property; it requires OpenZFS 2.3 or later, first available in FreeBSD 15.0.\n"
"See crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-deduplication,Deduplication] for details."
msgstr "校验和可用于在写入数据时检测重复块。启用重复数据删除后，已有相同块的引用计数会增加，从而节省存储空间。ZFS 会在内存中维护重复数据删除表（DDT），以检测重复块。该表包含唯一校验和列表、这些块的位置以及引用计数。写入新数据时，ZFS 会计算校验和并与列表进行比较。找到匹配项时，便会使用已有块。对重复数据删除使用 SHA256 校验和算法可提供安全的加密哈希。重复数据删除可以调整配置。若 `dedup` 为 `on`，匹配的校验和即表示数据相同。将 `dedup` 设为 `verify` 时，ZFS 会逐字节检查数据，确保数据确实相同。如果数据不同，ZFS 会记录哈希冲突，并分别存储这两个块。由于 DDT 必须存储每个唯一块的哈希，因此会占用大量内存。一个常见的经验法则是：每 1 TB 去重数据需要 5-6 GB RAM。如果实际条件不允许准备足够的 RAM 来将整个 DDT 保留在内存中，性能会大幅下降，因为每次写入新块之前，DDT 都必须从磁盘读取。重复数据删除可以使用 L2ARC 存储 DDT，在速度较快的系统内存与较慢的磁盘之间提供折衷方案。可以考虑改用压缩；它通常能节省近乎相同的空间，而且不会增加内存占用。\n__快速重复数据删除__会将 DDT 更新批量写入日志，允许使用 `zpool ddtprune` 清除过期条目，并通过池属性 `dedup_table_quota` 限制表的大小；此功能需要 OpenZFS 2.3 或更高版本，最早在 FreeBSD 15.0 中提供。\n详情请参见 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-deduplication,重复数据删除]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4406
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-block-cloning]]Block Cloning"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-block-cloning]]块克隆"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4411
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Block cloning allows a file copy to reference the existing on-disk blocks of the source file instead of duplicating them, so the copy completes almost instantly and consumes no extra space until either file changes.\n"
"On FreeBSD, man:cp[1] uses man:copy_file_range[2], so ordinary file copies become block clones when the feature is enabled (the default on FreeBSD 15.0).\n"
"The `bcloneused`, `bclonesaved`, and `bcloneratio` pool properties report the resulting space savings.\n"
"See crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-block-cloning,Block Cloning] for details."
msgstr "块克隆允许文件副本引用源文件已有的磁盘块，而不是重复复制这些块，因此复制几乎可以瞬间完成；在任一文件发生更改之前，副本都不会额外占用空间。\n在 FreeBSD 上，man:cp[1] 使用 man:copy_file_range[2]，因此启用此功能后（FreeBSD 15.0 默认启用），普通文件复制会成为块克隆。\n池属性 `bcloneused`、`bclonesaved` 和 `bcloneratio` 会报告由此节省的空间。\n详情请参见 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-block-cloning,块克隆]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4412
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-scrub]]Scrub"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-scrub]]数据清理"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4423
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Instead of a consistency check like man:fsck[8], ZFS has `scrub`. `scrub` reads\n"
"all data blocks stored on the pool and verifies their checksums against the\n"
"known good checksums stored in the metadata. A periodic check of all the data\n"
"stored on the pool ensures the recovery of any corrupted blocks before needing\n"
"them. A scrub is not required after an unclean shutdown, but good practice is at\n"
"least once every month. ZFS verifies the checksum of each block during\n"
"normal use, but a scrub makes certain to check even infrequently used blocks for\n"
"silent corruption. ZFS improves data security in archival storage situations.\n"
"Pause a running scrub with `zpool scrub -p` and resume it later by running `zpool scrub` again.\n"
"See crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-scrub,Scrubbing a Pool] for details."
msgstr "ZFS 使用 `scrub`，而不是像 man:fsck[8] 那样进行一致性检查。`scrub` 会读取池中存储的所有数据块，并将其校验和与元数据中存储的已知正确校验和进行验证。定期检查池中存储的所有数据，可确保在需要使用之前恢复任何已损坏的块。非正常关机后不必执行数据清理，但良好的做法是至少每月执行一次。ZFS 在正常使用过程中会验证每个块的校验和，而数据清理则确保检查到使用频率较低的块，以发现静默损坏。ZFS 可提高归档存储场景下的数据安全性。\n使用 `zpool scrub -p` 可暂停正在运行的数据清理，之后再次运行 `zpool scrub` 即可恢复。\n详情请参见 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-scrub,清理池]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4424
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-checkpoint]]Checkpoint"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-checkpoint]]检查点"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4429
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A checkpoint preserves the entire state of a pool at a single point in time, including pool-wide configuration changes that snapshots cannot capture.\n"
"Rewinding to a checkpoint with `zpool import --rewind-to-checkpoint` undoes everything that happened after taking it, such as enabling pool features, adding or removing vdevs, or destroying datasets.\n"
"A pool has at most one checkpoint at a time.\n"
"See crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-checkpoint,Pool Checkpoints] for details."
msgstr "检查点会保留池在某个时间点的完整状态，包括快照无法捕获的池级配置更改。\n使用 `zpool import --rewind-to-checkpoint` 回滚到检查点，会撤销创建检查点之后发生的一切操作，例如启用池功能、添加或移除 vdev，或销毁数据集。\n一个池同一时间最多只能有一个检查点。\n详情请参见 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-checkpoint,池检查点]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4430
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-trim]]TRIM"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-trim]]TRIM"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4434
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"TRIM notifies SSDs and other flash-based storage which blocks the pool no longer uses, allowing the device to erase them in advance and sustain write performance.\n"
"Run `zpool trim` manually, or set the `autotrim` pool property to `on` to trim freed space continuously.\n"
"See crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-trim,TRIM and Initialization] for details."
msgstr "TRIM 会通知 SSD 和其他基于闪存的存储设备池中哪些块已不再使用，使设备可以提前擦除这些块并维持写入性能。\n可以手动运行 `zpool trim`，也可以将池属性 `autotrim` 设为 `on`，以便持续 TRIM 已释放的空间。\n详情请参见 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-trim,TRIM 与初始化]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4435
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-quota]]Dataset Quota"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-quota]]数据集配额"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4449
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"ZFS provides fast and accurate dataset, user, and group space accounting as well as quotas and space reservations. This gives the administrator fine grained control over space allocation and allows reserving space for critical file systems.\n"
"\n"
"ZFS supports different types of quotas: the dataset quota, the\n"
"crossref:zfs[zfs-term-refquota,reference quota (refquota)], the\n"
"crossref:zfs[zfs-term-userquota,user quota], and the\n"
"crossref:zfs[zfs-term-groupquota,group quota].\n"
"\n"
"Quotas limit the total size of a dataset and its descendants, including snapshots of the dataset, child datasets, and the snapshots of those datasets.\n"
"\n"
"[NOTE]\n"
"====\n"
"Volumes do not support quotas, as the `volsize` property acts as an implicit quota.\n"
"===="
msgstr "ZFS 可快速、准确地统计数据集、用户和组的空间使用情况，并支持配额和空间预留。这让管理员可以精细控制空间分配，并为关键文件系统预留空间。\n\nZFS 支持多种配额：数据集配额、crossref:zfs[zfs-term-refquota,引用配额（refquota）]、crossref:zfs[zfs-term-userquota,用户配额]和 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-groupquota,组配额]。\n\n配额限制数据集及其后代所占用的总空间，包括该数据集的快照、子数据集以及这些子数据集的快照。\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n卷不支持配额，因为 `volsize` 属性相当于隐式配额。\n===="

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4450
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-refquota]]Reference Quota"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-refquota]]引用配额"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4452
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "A reference quota limits the amount of space a dataset can consume by enforcing a hard limit. This hard limit includes space referenced by the dataset alone and does not include space used by descendants, such as file systems or snapshots."
msgstr "引用配额通过实施硬性上限，限制数据集可占用的空间量。此上限仅包括数据集本身引用的空间，不包括后代（例如文件系统或快照）使用的空间。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4453
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-userquota]]User Quota"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-userquota]]用户配额"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4455
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "User quotas are useful to limit the amount of space used by the specified user."
msgstr "用户配额可用于限制指定用户使用的空间量。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4456
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-groupquota]]Group Quota"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-groupquota]]组配额"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4458
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "The group quota limits the amount of space that a specified group can consume."
msgstr "组配额限制指定组可占用的空间量。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4459
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-reservation]]Dataset Reservation"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-reservation]]数据集预留"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4467
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `reservation` property makes it possible to guarantee an amount of space\n"
"for a specific dataset and its descendants. This means that setting a 10 GB\n"
"reservation on [.filename]#storage/home/bob# prevents other datasets from using\n"
"up all free space, reserving at least 10 GB of space for this dataset. Unlike a\n"
"regular crossref:zfs[zfs-term-refreservation,`refreservation`], space used by snapshots and descendant datasets does count against the reservation.\n"
"\n"
"Reservations of any sort are useful in situations such as planning and testing the suitability of disk space allocation in a new system, or ensuring that enough space is available on file systems for audio logs or system recovery procedures and files."
msgstr "`reservation` 属性可为特定数据集及其后代保证一定量的空间。这意味着，在 [.filename]#storage/home/bob# 上设置 10 GB 的预留，可防止其他数据集耗尽所有可用空间，并为该数据集至少保留 10 GB 空间。与常规的 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-refreservation,`refreservation`] 不同，快照和后代数据集使用的空间会计入预留。\n\n各种预留在多种场景下都很有用，例如规划和测试新系统中的磁盘空间分配是否合适，或确保文件系统有足够空间用于音频日志或系统恢复流程及文件。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4468
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-refreservation]]Reference Reservation"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-refreservation]]引用预留"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4474
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `refreservation` property makes it possible to guarantee an amount of space\n"
"for the use of a specific dataset _excluding_ its descendants. This means that\n"
"setting a 10 GB reservation on [.filename]#storage/home/bob#, and another\n"
"dataset tries to use the free space, reserving at least 10 GB of space for this\n"
"dataset. In contrast to a regular crossref:zfs[zfs-term-reservation,reservation], space used by snapshots and descendant datasets is not counted against the reservation. For example, if taking a snapshot of [.filename]#storage/home/bob#, enough disk space other than the `refreservation` amount must exist for the operation to succeed. Descendants of the main data set are not counted in the `refreservation` amount and so do not encroach on the space set."
msgstr "`refreservation` 属性可为特定数据集保证一定量的可用空间，__不包括__其后代。这意味着，在 [.filename]#storage/home/bob# 上设置 10 GB 的预留后，即使另一个数据集尝试使用可用空间，也会为该数据集至少保留 10 GB。与常规的 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-reservation,reservation] 不同，快照和后代数据集使用的空间不会计入该预留。例如，如果要为 [.filename]#storage/home/bob# 创建快照，除 `refreservation` 预留的空间外，还必须有足够的磁盘空间才能成功完成操作。主数据集的后代不计入 `refreservation` 的额度，因此不会侵占预留空间。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4475
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-boot-environment]]Boot Environment"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-boot-environment]]引导环境"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4479
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A boot environment is a bootable clone of the datasets that hold the FreeBSD system, managed with man:bectl[8].\n"
"Creating a boot environment before a system upgrade makes it possible to boot the previous, known-good system from the loader menu if the upgrade causes problems.\n"
"See crossref:zfs[zfs-boot-environments,Boot Environments] for details."
msgstr "引导环境是保存 FreeBSD 系统的数据集的可引导克隆，由 man:bectl[8] 管理。\n在系统升级前创建引导环境，可在升级出现问题时，从 loader 菜单启动先前已知正常的系统。\n详情请参见 crossref:zfs[zfs-boot-environments,引导环境]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4480
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-resilver]]Resilver"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-resilver]]重建冗余"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4486
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When replacing a failed disk, ZFS must fill the new disk with the lost data.\n"
"_Resilvering_ is the process of writing that data to the replacement device: mirrors resilver by copying the data from the surviving members, while RAID-Z reconstructs it from the parity information distributed across the remaining drives.\n"
"Unlike a traditional RAID rebuild, resilvering copies allocated data alone rather than every sector of the device.\n"
"A _sequential resilver_ (`zpool attach -s` or `zpool replace -s`) rebuilds mirror and dRAID vdevs even faster by copying blocks in disk order, skipping checksum verification and deferring it to an automatically scheduled scrub.\n"
"See crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-resilver,Dealing with Failed Devices] for details."
msgstr "更换故障磁盘时，ZFS 必须将丢失的数据填充到新磁盘上。\n__重建冗余__是将这些数据写入替换设备的过程：镜像通过从仍正常工作的成员复制数据来重建冗余，而 RAID-Z 则根据分布在剩余磁盘上的奇偶校验信息进行重建。\n与传统 RAID 重建不同，重建冗余只复制已分配的数据，而不是设备的每个扇区。\n__顺序重建冗余__（`zpool attach -s` 或 `zpool replace -s`）会按磁盘顺序复制块，从而更快地重建镜像和 dRAID vdev；它会跳过校验和验证，并将验证推迟到自动安排的数据清理中。\n详情请参见 crossref:zfs[zfs-zpool-resilver,处理故障设备]。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4487
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-online]]Online"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-online]]在线"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4489
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "A pool or vdev in the `Online` state has its member devices connected and fully operational. Individual devices in the `Online` state are functioning."
msgstr "处于 `Online` 状态的池或 vdev，其成员设备均已连接且运行正常。处于 `Online` 状态的单个设备也均正常运行。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4490
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-offline]]Offline"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-offline]]离线"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4494
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The administrator puts individual devices in an `Offline` state if enough\n"
"redundancy exists to avoid putting the pool or vdev into a\n"
"crossref:zfs[zfs-term-faulted,Faulted] state. An administrator may choose to offline a disk in preparation for replacing it, or to make it easier to identify."
msgstr "如果冗余足以避免池或 vdev 进入 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-faulted,故障]状态，管理员可以将单个设备设为 `Offline` 状态。管理员可以选择在更换磁盘前将其设为离线，或以便于识别该磁盘。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4495
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-degraded]]Degraded"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-degraded]]降级"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4502
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A pool or vdev in the `Degraded` state has one or more disks that disappeared\n"
"or failed. The pool is still usable, but if other devices fail, the pool may\n"
"become unrecoverable. Reconnecting the missing devices or replacing the failed\n"
"disks will return the pool to an crossref:zfs[zfs-term-online,Online] state\n"
"after the reconnected or new device has completed the\n"
"crossref:zfs[zfs-term-resilver,Resilver] process."
msgstr "处于 `Degraded` 状态的池或 vdev 中有一个或多个磁盘已消失或发生故障。池仍可使用，但如果其他设备也发生故障，池可能会变得无法恢复。重新连接缺失设备或更换故障磁盘后，待重新连接的设备或新设备完成 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-resilver,重建冗余]，池便会恢复到 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-online,在线]状态。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4503
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-faulted]]Faulted"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-faulted]]故障"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4509
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A pool or vdev in the `Faulted` state is no longer operational. Accessing the\n"
"data is no longer possible. A pool or vdev enters the `Faulted` state when the\n"
"number of missing or failed devices exceeds the level of redundancy in the vdev.\n"
"If reconnecting missing devices the pool will return to an\n"
"crossref:zfs[zfs-term-online,Online] state. Insufficient redundancy to compensate for the number of failed disks loses the pool contents and requires restoring from backups."
msgstr "处于 `Faulted` 状态的池或 vdev 已无法运行，数据也无法访问。当缺失或故障设备的数量超过 vdev 的冗余级别时，池或 vdev 就会进入 `Faulted` 状态。如果重新连接缺失设备，池将恢复到 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-online,在线]状态。如果冗余不足以补偿故障磁盘的数量，池内容就会丢失，必须从备份恢复。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4510
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-unavail]]Unavail"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-unavail]]不可用"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4514
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A device in the `Unavail` state cannot be opened, because it is missing or inaccessible.\n"
"The pool continues operating if enough redundancy exists to compensate, running in a crossref:zfs[zfs-term-degraded,Degraded] state.\n"
"If a top-level vdev is `Unavail`, accessing the pool contents is impossible."
msgstr "处于 `Unavail` 状态的设备无法打开，因为它已缺失或无法访问。\n如果冗余足以进行补偿，池会继续运行并处于 crossref:zfs[zfs-term-degraded,降级]状态。\n如果顶层 vdev 处于 `Unavail` 状态，则无法访问池内容。"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4515
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "[[zfs-term-removed]]Removed"
msgstr "[[zfs-term-removed]]已移除"

#. type: Table
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/zfs/_index.adoc:4518
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A device in the `Removed` state was physically detached while the system was running.\n"
"Device removal detection is hardware-dependent and unsupported on some platforms.\n"
"When the device reconnects, man:zfsd[8] brings it back online; if the device does not return, zfsd activates an available hot spare in its place."
msgstr "处于 `Removed` 状态的设备是在系统运行时被物理断开的。\n设备移除检测取决于硬件，且某些平台不支持此功能。\n设备重新连接后，man:zfsd[8] 会使其恢复在线；如果设备未重新连接，zfsd 会启用一个可用的热备盘来替代它。"

